14
00:00:43,578 --> 00:00:45,478
and work for three hours.

15
00:00:46,648 --> 00:00:48,348
Team Land...

16
00:00:48,478 --> 00:00:49,748
will leave at 4am...

17
00:00:49,948 --> 00:00:52,018
and work for two hours.

18
00:00:52,118 --> 00:00:54,118
Please, Team Land.

19
00:00:54,988 --> 00:00:56,288
It's too different.

20
00:00:57,758 --> 00:01:00,728
- So, how should we do this? - So, again, we will...

21
00:01:01,098 --> 00:01:03,057
- Oh, a random draw again... - So?

22
00:01:03,058 --> 00:01:04,497
- Are we doing something now? - We're going to drink that again.

23
00:01:04,498 --> 00:01:06,378
- It's a game. - No, I don't like random draws.

24
00:01:06,668 --> 00:01:10,098
- I really don't want to do it. - So some people will go Team Sea...

25
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:14,408
(After being sent off on sea squirt duty upon arrival)

26
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:16,237
(Sea squirt, onion, )

27
00:01:16,238 --> 00:01:18,308
(chicken farm, green plum)

28
00:01:18,808 --> 00:01:21,948
(She achieved a grand slam of extra work.)

29
00:01:22,518 --> 00:01:25,718
(The unluckiest person on Fresh off the Sea)

30
00:01:25,918 --> 00:01:28,458
It'll be so unfair if I don't get put on Team Land.

31
00:01:29,488 --> 00:01:32,287
We'll do a random draw again.

32
00:01:32,288 --> 00:01:33,358
Random draw.

33
00:01:33,998 --> 00:01:35,727
I have a bad feeling about this.

34
00:01:35,728 --> 00:01:36,798
Okay.

35
00:01:37,768 --> 00:01:38,968
I like random draws.

36
00:01:39,598 --> 00:01:40,667
They're fun.

37
00:01:40,668 --> 00:01:43,138
(What lies in their futures?)

38
00:01:44,168 --> 00:01:47,478
If I get unlucky again this time, it'll be legendary.

39
00:01:51,048 --> 00:01:53,208
(The hot sun disappears out of view.)

40
00:01:53,478 --> 00:01:54,548
Let's do this.

41
00:01:55,278 --> 00:01:57,247
- What could it be? - I saw them bring something in.

42
00:01:57,248 --> 00:01:58,347
I was wondering what it was.

43
00:01:58,348 --> 00:01:59,647
(What is today's random draw?)

44
00:01:59,648 --> 00:02:00,718
What is it?

45
00:02:00,958 --> 00:02:02,188
There's a rope.

46
00:02:02,658 --> 00:02:04,128
You put this around your waist.

47
00:02:04,188 --> 00:02:05,858
Oh, I have no strength.

48
00:02:06,388 --> 00:02:08,428
Is this a random draw? What is this?

49
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:10,468
- Should we put them on first? - Yes.

50
00:02:10,798 --> 00:02:12,097
- Just put it around my waist? - Yes.

51
00:02:12,098 --> 00:02:13,838
(Putting the belts on without knowing why)

52
00:02:14,838 --> 00:02:16,738
Attach only one rope to a motorcycle...

53
00:02:17,808 --> 00:02:19,008
- Until the end. - Is that it?

54
00:02:19,368 --> 00:02:21,308
Hello, I'm Jeong Sang Hun. Oh, my!

55
00:02:22,278 --> 00:02:24,607
I feel like this is going to be very funny.

56
00:02:24,608 --> 00:02:25,808
Does this require strength?

57
00:02:26,008 --> 00:02:27,918
- Oh, gosh. - Could this be...

58
00:02:28,548 --> 00:02:31,388
Are you putting these on fire?

59
00:02:31,848 --> 00:02:33,318
If the fire comes to you...

60
00:02:34,818 --> 00:02:35,818
You lose.

61
00:02:35,819 --> 00:02:38,427
(The human fuse random draw)

62
00:02:38,428 --> 00:02:40,798
(That's not it, of course.)

63
00:02:41,058 --> 00:02:42,998
I think it's kind of like the ladder game.

64
00:02:43,798 --> 00:02:45,398
A human ladder.

65
00:02:45,898 --> 00:02:48,238
"Who's going?" They'll pull one, and if you get pulled...

66
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:49,737
Okay.

67
00:02:49,738 --> 00:02:51,667
To explain one more time,

68
00:02:51,668 --> 00:02:55,708
tomorrow, two people will go to do work on the sea,

69
00:02:55,938 --> 00:02:58,377
and three people will go to do work on land.

70
00:02:58,378 --> 00:03:02,418
So we have invited a special guest.

71
00:03:02,748 --> 00:03:06,087
It's someone Jung Ah has worked with before.

72
00:03:06,088 --> 00:03:08,218
Captain Ju Jin Su will...

73
00:03:08,918 --> 00:03:10,627
(The captain of the fixed net fishing boat...)

74
00:03:10,628 --> 00:03:12,357
(from Season 2 Episode 13)

75
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:14,028
He will choose Team Sea...

76
00:03:14,228 --> 00:03:15,327
- Oh, in Yeosu? - Yes.

77
00:03:15,328 --> 00:03:17,098
He will choose that team.

78
00:03:17,198 --> 00:03:19,697
The Village Chief...

79
00:03:19,698 --> 00:03:22,468
will choose Team Land.

80
00:03:22,968 --> 00:03:24,808
Village Chief, please.

81
00:03:25,138 --> 00:03:26,838
- Village Chief, please. - Okay.

82
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:29,407
- Hello. - Hello.

83
00:03:29,408 --> 00:03:30,408
Hello.

84
00:03:30,409 --> 00:03:32,477
- Oh, Actress Yum. - Hello.

85
00:03:32,478 --> 00:03:34,224
(Ju Jin Su, Captain, Park Young Uk, Village Chief)

86
00:03:34,248 --> 00:03:35,618
Hello.

87
00:03:36,048 --> 00:03:37,388
Please choose well.

88
00:03:37,648 --> 00:03:39,118
Village Chief and Captain.

89
00:03:39,588 --> 00:03:42,358
Captain, you'll go first.

90
00:03:42,788 --> 00:03:45,488
Pull a rope to choose the first person...

91
00:03:46,028 --> 00:03:47,127
who will go to the sea.

92
00:03:47,128 --> 00:03:50,828
(The person who is chosen will be 1 of 2 Team Sea members.)

93
00:03:51,598 --> 00:03:53,968
(Will we have to take off at 3am...)

94
00:03:54,738 --> 00:03:58,708
(and work on the rough ocean?)

95
00:04:01,738 --> 00:04:04,007
(Fate...)

96
00:04:04,008 --> 00:04:06,148
(has been sealed.)

97
00:04:09,748 --> 00:04:11,217
(Welcome...)

98
00:04:11,218 --> 00:04:13,348
(to Yeosu Sea!)

99
00:04:14,758 --> 00:04:16,518
Oh, it's me!

100
00:04:18,228 --> 00:04:20,628
(Oh, it's me... It's me!)

101
00:04:20,898 --> 00:04:22,558
(Laughing)

102
00:04:22,958 --> 00:04:25,128
(I survived.)

103
00:04:25,768 --> 00:04:27,798
It's me. It's me!

104
00:04:28,638 --> 00:04:30,268
I really can't go to the sea.

105
00:04:30,638 --> 00:04:31,707
Seriously.

106
00:04:31,708 --> 00:04:33,008
(Have fun.)

107
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:34,707
I didn't know I'd be chosen on the first go.

108
00:04:34,708 --> 00:04:36,007
- How about this, then? - A 40 percent chance...

109
00:04:36,008 --> 00:04:37,207
For Team Land and Team Sea...

110
00:04:37,208 --> 00:04:38,677
Please choose one person...

111
00:04:38,678 --> 00:04:41,148
for Team Land to work in the field.

112
00:04:41,318 --> 00:04:43,577
In the field? Okay, in the field.

113
00:04:43,578 --> 00:04:44,648
Who will it be?

114
00:04:45,288 --> 00:04:47,758
(Please let it be me!)

115
00:04:47,888 --> 00:04:49,187
- That would be nice. - Here I go.

116
00:04:49,188 --> 00:04:50,218
Okay.

117
00:04:51,188 --> 00:04:52,257
Let's see.

118
00:04:52,258 --> 00:04:53,388
What?

119
00:04:56,258 --> 00:04:59,828
(What?)

120
00:05:00,368 --> 00:05:03,298
Why are you so strong, Chief?

121
00:05:04,768 --> 00:05:06,037
I'm working in the field.

122
00:05:06,038 --> 00:05:07,678
(Sang Hun got picked to be on Team Land.)

123
00:05:07,908 --> 00:05:09,108
How about this, then?

124
00:05:09,178 --> 00:05:11,507
Since we have one person for Team Land and Team Sea,

125
00:05:11,508 --> 00:05:12,708
