126
00:05:13,048 --> 00:05:14,618
I want to pick who comes with me.

127
00:05:15,048 --> 00:05:16,378
Right, from field work.

128
00:05:16,478 --> 00:05:18,518
Then you pick one, and then I'll pick the last one.

129
00:05:19,118 --> 00:05:22,087
No, don't do that. I'd prefer the Village Chief and...

130
00:05:22,088 --> 00:05:23,688
- and the Captain to choose. - Yoon Seo.

131
00:05:23,828 --> 00:05:26,087
- I'll have less resentment, then. - Yoon Seo, I'll pick you.

132
00:05:26,088 --> 00:05:28,497
No, let's not do this.

133
00:05:28,498 --> 00:05:30,328
I'd rather have them pick.

134
00:05:31,798 --> 00:05:32,868
Okay.

135
00:05:34,368 --> 00:05:35,768
Which one is it this time?

136
00:05:35,968 --> 00:05:39,508
- This time, we have three ropes. - Yes.

137
00:05:39,808 --> 00:05:41,168
We'll pick the field worker first.

138
00:05:42,038 --> 00:05:44,808
Jung Ah. Pick one of these three. Which one?

139
00:05:45,278 --> 00:05:46,348
You don't want to pick?

140
00:05:47,078 --> 00:05:48,148
Yoon Seo?

141
00:05:49,818 --> 00:05:50,918
The one on the left.

142
00:05:51,388 --> 00:05:52,687
- The one on the left? - This one.

143
00:05:52,688 --> 00:05:53,918
This one? Oh, the other side.

144
00:05:54,288 --> 00:05:56,318
This side. I'll pick this one.

145
00:05:57,258 --> 00:06:00,488
I don't think it's me. Oh, no...

146
00:06:01,328 --> 00:06:02,798
- Who will it be? - Okay.

147
00:06:03,158 --> 00:06:05,928
Here we go. Come on.

148
00:06:06,168 --> 00:06:07,238
Congratulations.

149
00:06:08,168 --> 00:06:09,498
- Okay. - Congratulations.

150
00:06:10,038 --> 00:06:11,607
- It'll start moving now. - We don't know yet.

151
00:06:11,608 --> 00:06:13,468
- It's Sun Young. - We don't know yet.

152
00:06:14,438 --> 00:06:17,308
(Will Lady Luck be on Sun Young's side once again?)

153
00:06:17,808 --> 00:06:19,547
- We don't know yet. What? - What?

154
00:06:19,548 --> 00:06:21,548
Oh, it's moving now.

155
00:06:23,318 --> 00:06:24,788
(Flinching)

156
00:06:26,248 --> 00:06:27,358
(Gasping)

157
00:06:27,788 --> 00:06:28,858
I think it's me!

158
00:06:29,918 --> 00:06:30,958
I think it's me!

159
00:06:31,328 --> 00:06:33,028
(Please.)

160
00:06:33,658 --> 00:06:37,298
(Who will be the second member of Team Land?)

161
00:06:37,998 --> 00:06:39,068
Is it me?

162
00:06:39,368 --> 00:06:40,427
Is it me? Really?

163
00:06:40,428 --> 00:06:42,267
(Unlucky Yoon Seo was picked.)

164
00:06:42,268 --> 00:06:44,138
She chose the rope and got picked.

165
00:06:44,838 --> 00:06:47,138
- This is new! - I picked it!

166
00:06:47,238 --> 00:06:48,707
(I can't believe I did it...)

167
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:50,108
I picked my own.

168
00:06:50,478 --> 00:06:53,378
Finally, at the end. I'm so happy.

169
00:06:53,648 --> 00:06:54,817
I think I'm going to cry.

170
00:06:54,818 --> 00:06:56,118
(Overjoyed)

171
00:06:56,818 --> 00:06:58,417
Now it's Team Sea, right?

172
00:06:58,418 --> 00:06:59,864
(One of these two will be on Team Sea.)

173
00:06:59,888 --> 00:07:02,618
Which of you wants to come with me? Let me hear you scream!

174
00:07:03,358 --> 00:07:06,058
Which of you wants to come with me? Let me hear you scream!

175
00:07:08,128 --> 00:07:09,327
(I'll go.)

176
00:07:09,328 --> 00:07:10,427
She says she wants to go.

177
00:07:10,428 --> 00:07:11,497
- Really? - Yes.

178
00:07:11,498 --> 00:07:12,568
Pick me.

179
00:07:13,528 --> 00:07:14,897
- Then I'll pick this one. - Okay.

180
00:07:14,898 --> 00:07:16,618
(So he chooses the rope on Jung Ah's side.)

181
00:07:16,668 --> 00:07:18,548
The person who'll come to the sea with me is...

182
00:07:20,068 --> 00:07:23,777
(Who did You Seok's heart go to?)

183
00:07:23,778 --> 00:07:24,808
The stick of love.

184
00:07:31,348 --> 00:07:33,958
(Overwhelmed with emotion)

185
00:07:37,388 --> 00:07:38,427
Sun Young.

186
00:07:38,428 --> 00:07:39,527
(Congratulations to the sea couple.)

187
00:07:39,528 --> 00:07:40,528
Welcome to...

188
00:07:41,358 --> 00:07:45,098
(Our grasshopper couple came to be in Taean.)

189
00:07:45,898 --> 00:07:47,667
(We have a good energy. We should stick together.)

190
00:07:47,668 --> 00:07:49,468
(Yes.)

191
00:07:50,038 --> 00:07:51,038
Sun Young.

192
00:07:51,039 --> 00:07:52,237
(You are my destiny.)

193
00:07:52,238 --> 00:07:53,268
Welcome to...

194
00:07:55,008 --> 00:07:57,038
(Dying of happiness)

195
00:07:57,578 --> 00:07:59,878
(Jung Ah is automatically on Team Land.)

196
00:08:01,448 --> 00:08:02,518
Thank you.

197
00:08:03,478 --> 00:08:05,047
- Thank you, Chief and Captain. - Thank you.

198
00:08:05,048 --> 00:08:06,348
(We'll be going now.)

199
00:08:07,048 --> 00:08:08,057
This game is fun.

200
00:08:08,058 --> 00:08:10,234
- I feel like we need to do more. - Let's play it one more time.

201
00:08:10,258 --> 00:08:11,828
- Maybe for the dishes? - Yes.

202
00:08:12,258 --> 00:08:14,458
- No, let's wash up and sleep. - She wants to sleep.

203
00:08:15,658 --> 00:08:16,658
(Sure, let's sleep...)

204
00:08:16,659 --> 00:08:17,798
Let's sleep.

205
00:08:18,268 --> 00:08:19,398
Okay, then. Tomorrow,

206
00:08:20,068 --> 00:08:23,537
Sun Young and You Seok, you two will go to the sea.

207
00:08:23,538 --> 00:08:26,367
Jung Ah, Sang Hun, and Yoon Seo, the three of you...

208
00:08:26,368 --> 00:08:27,878
- will stay on land. - Okay.

209
00:08:28,208 --> 00:08:30,778
- What about the uniform? - Let's take off

210
00:08:31,148 --> 00:08:33,308
- All of us? Then we... - The two of us

211
00:08:33,678 --> 00:08:34,817
I'm so overjoyed.

212
00:08:34,818 --> 00:08:36,218
(Crying)

213
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:40,958
- Yoon Seo, come to the sea with me. - What are you saying?

214
00:08:42,858 --> 00:08:45,357
- Let's wash up. - I'll go first.

215
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:46,458
- Okay. - Okay.

216
00:08:47,958 --> 00:08:49,128
Oh, gosh.

217
00:08:50,328 --> 00:08:52,467
Oh, gosh. Good work, everyone.

218
00:08:52,468 --> 00:08:54,198
- Good work. - Let's sleep.

219
00:08:54,668 --> 00:08:56,638
Oh, how nice.

220
00:08:59,608 --> 00:09:02,078
(Everyone heads to bed at 9pm.)

221
00:09:02,678 --> 00:09:05,008
(Darkness has come over Yeosu's dawn sky.)

222
00:09:12,318 --> 00:09:15,258
(Sun Young of Team Sea is already up?)

223
00:09:16,918 --> 00:09:20,588
(Her nerves woke her up.)

224
00:09:22,258 --> 00:09:24,298
(Should I start getting ready?)

225
00:09:25,328 --> 00:09:27,868
(She quickly washes her face.)

226
00:09:29,268 --> 00:09:30,368
You Seok.

227
00:09:31,208 --> 00:09:32,308
- You Seok? - Yes?

228
00:09:33,238 --> 00:09:36,438
(Still half asleep, You Seok gets up at Sun Young's morning call.)

229
00:09:36,878 --> 00:09:39,608
I'm worried I'll get seasick if I go on an empty stomach.

230
00:09:40,508 --> 00:09:41,517
Should we put on some patches?

231
00:09:41,518 --> 00:09:42,758
(Worried about getting seasick)

232
00:09:43,978 --> 00:09:47,088
(A bit nervous about working on a boat so early in the morning)

233
00:09:47,458 --> 00:09:48,488
(Sighing)

234
00:09:49,418 --> 00:09:50,517
Do you know what time it is, everyone?

235
00:09:50,518 --> 00:09:51,587
(Current time: 2:30am)

236
00:09:51,588 --> 00:09:53,057
I'm so out of it right now.

237
00:09:53,058 --> 00:09:54,097
(You Seok can't believe he will get on a boat right after waking up.)

238
00:09:54,098 --> 00:09:55,997
I feel like I'm dreaming right now, everyone.

239
00:09:55,998 --> 00:09:57,274
(You Seok can't believe he will get on a boat right after waking up.)

240
00:09:57,298 --> 00:09:59,728
(Meanwhile, at the harbor, )

241
00:10:00,838 --> 00:10:04,338
(everyone is getting ready to set sail.)

242
00:10:06,268 --> 00:10:10,008
(Several fishing boats have already sailed out into sea.)

243
00:10:11,348 --> 00:10:13,248
- Let's go. - This is a dream, right?

244
00:10:13,548 --> 00:10:14,868
- What? - This is a dream, right?

245
00:10:15,018 --> 00:10:16,677
(Current time, 2:40am, It still feels like he's dreaming.)

246
00:10:16,678 --> 00:10:19,018
(Spacing out)

247
00:10:19,188 --> 00:10:22,158
Can you see out in sea in this darkness?

248
00:10:22,758 --> 00:10:24,478
- They'll probably turn on lights. - Right.

249
00:10:26,288 --> 00:10:27,288
What do you think it'll be today?

250
00:10:27,289 --> 00:10:28,297
(She's curious what sort of work they'll do today.)

251
00:10:28,298 --> 00:10:30,997
Have you been on a boat? No, right? On one like this.

252
00:10:30,998 --> 00:10:32,168
Not at this hour.

253
00:10:33,968 --> 00:10:35,837
After one episode aired...

254
00:10:35,838 --> 00:10:37,297
(The day before, the first episode of Fresh off the Sea 3 had aired.)

255
00:10:37,298 --> 00:10:39,738
- It was... - Everyone liked it, right?

256
00:10:39,838 --> 00:10:41,084
- You Seok. - They all loved it.

257
00:10:41,108 --> 00:10:44,608
On our family chatroom, my sister wrote like ten lines...

258
00:10:45,178 --> 00:10:46,178
What did she say?

259
00:10:47,208 --> 00:10:50,047
"Sun Young is so funny and totally my style. ENFP."

260
00:10:50,048 --> 00:10:52,187
"Laugh out loud. Just watching is so fun."

261
00:10:52,188 --> 00:10:53,918
"Sun Young is so like me. She's so funny."

262
00:10:54,158 --> 00:10:56,888
Your sister's personality is like me?

263
00:10:56,988 --> 00:10:58,027
(Thinking)

264
00:10:58,028 --> 00:11:00,488
But in my opinion, my sister isn't funny.

265
00:11:01,958 --> 00:11:03,758
(The cold judgment of a sibling)

266
00:11:04,028 --> 00:11:06,168
"Yoon Seo is so pretty and nice and perfect."

267
00:11:06,698 --> 00:11:08,268
Yoon Seo...

268
00:11:08,798 --> 00:11:11,638
looks like a city girl,

269
00:11:11,868 --> 00:11:15,507
but she's so laid-back and positive.

270
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,508
Right.

271
00:11:16,708 --> 00:11:19,648
Through this program,

272
00:11:20,948 --> 00:11:23,848
I really grew to like both you and Yoon Seo.

273
00:11:24,078 --> 00:11:27,388
You two are great. I'm glad you joined this program.

274
00:11:28,558 --> 00:11:29,957
Yoon Seo too. Seriously.

275
00:11:29,958 --> 00:11:30,988
(Sun Young is the best.)

276
00:11:31,228 --> 00:11:33,788
The two youngsters are so lovely.

277
00:11:34,358 --> 00:11:35,397
Both of them.

278
00:11:35,398 --> 00:11:37,398
We were never awkward with each other,

279
00:11:37,498 --> 00:11:39,668
even on the first day we met.

280
00:11:40,768 --> 00:11:43,767
Even on the first day we met, we attacked each other.

281
00:11:43,768 --> 00:11:46,088
(Even on their first day on set, they were like siblings.)

282
00:11:48,838 --> 00:11:51,048
Everyone watching at home. Didn't I become prettier?

283
00:11:51,548 --> 00:11:53,078
(Giggling)

284
00:11:53,778 --> 00:11:56,048
Don't my eyebrows look so nice?

285
00:11:56,248 --> 00:11:59,318
(Her communication is going well as usual.)

286
00:12:00,218 --> 00:12:01,487
(They already arrived at their destination.)

287
00:12:01,488 --> 00:12:02,518
It's the ocean.

288
00:12:03,988 --> 00:12:05,127
- Thank you. - Thank you.

289
00:12:05,128 --> 00:12:06,888
(What work will they do on the sea at dawn?)

290
00:12:07,658 --> 00:12:09,127
This is better than it being...

291
00:12:09,128 --> 00:12:10,598
- very sunny, right? - Yes.

292
00:12:11,598 --> 00:12:12,997
This is nice. It's not hot.

293
00:12:12,998 --> 00:12:16,168
(Unlike the pepper field yesterday, it's nice and cool.)

294
00:12:16,598 --> 00:12:17,637
My mood...

295
00:12:17,638 --> 00:12:18,837
(Current time: 3:20am)

296
00:12:18,838 --> 00:12:20,037
- It's getting better. - Yes.

297
00:12:20,038 --> 00:12:22,537
This is better than being under the sun. It's much better.

298
00:12:22,538 --> 00:12:24,848
(They can only see some lights on the fishing boats.)

299
00:12:25,278 --> 00:12:28,217
Once we start working, dopamine will start pumping.

300
00:12:28,218 --> 00:12:29,248
It'll be fun.

301
00:12:30,648 --> 00:12:33,487
- So what you two... - Yes.

302
00:12:33,488 --> 00:12:35,358
- will be doing today... - Yes.

303
00:12:35,788 --> 00:12:37,788
- Octopus. - A delicacy of the Yeosu Sea...

304
00:12:38,628 --> 00:12:41,058
(A delicacy of the Yeosu Sea...)

305
00:12:41,328 --> 00:12:42,858
- Gizzard shad. - Gizzard shad?

306
00:12:43,728 --> 00:12:46,268
- Fall gizzard shad. - Oh, Yeosu has gizzard shads?

307
00:12:48,098 --> 00:12:50,567
(They say even daughters-in-law who left home...)

308
00:12:50,568 --> 00:12:54,208
(come back at the smell of grilling this fish.)

309
00:12:54,938 --> 00:12:58,008
(A legendary seasonal fish, gizzard shad)

310
00:12:58,808 --> 00:13:02,178
In Yeosu, we're proud of our clean sea.

311
00:13:02,278 --> 00:13:05,888
It's long been a habitat for gizzard shad.

312
00:13:06,148 --> 00:13:07,917
I've caught gizzard shad all my life.

313
00:13:07,918 --> 00:13:09,364
(The clean Yeosu Sea is full of tasty gizzard shad.)

314
00:13:09,388 --> 00:13:12,888
It's tasty both grilled and raw.

315
00:13:13,258 --> 00:13:15,298
Gizzard shad tastes good any way you prepare it.

316
00:13:15,858 --> 00:13:16,898
It's so tasty.

317
00:13:17,528 --> 00:13:19,197
They'll keep coming from now.

318
00:13:19,198 --> 00:13:20,397
(From August to October)

319
00:13:20,398 --> 00:13:23,697
There's nothing better than gizzard shad.

320
00:13:23,698 --> 00:13:25,314
(From August to October, You can catch in-season gizzard shad.)

321
00:13:25,338 --> 00:13:27,508
(Let's head out to Yeosu's night sea.)

322
00:13:27,808 --> 00:13:30,207
- Okay. - Gizzard shad sashimi is tasty.

323
00:13:30,208 --> 00:13:31,208
Okay.

324
00:13:31,978 --> 00:13:34,248
Is anyone waiting on a daughter-in-law to come back?

325
00:13:34,748 --> 00:13:36,218
I'll get her to come back.

326
00:13:36,448 --> 00:13:38,118
It's your first time on a fishing boat.

327
00:13:38,948 --> 00:13:40,818
- It's my first time. - It'll be fun.

328
00:13:42,058 --> 00:13:43,338
Once we start working, it's fun.

329
00:13:44,428 --> 00:13:46,127
- You're catching them alive. - Exactly.

330
00:13:46,128 --> 00:13:48,698
(Excited about catching live fish)

331
00:13:48,998 --> 00:13:50,828
Sun Young. Be careful.

332
00:13:50,928 --> 00:13:52,567
Oh, my!

333
00:13:52,568 --> 00:13:53,598
This is no joke.

334
00:13:54,098 --> 00:13:55,567
(Even getting on the boat is hard.)

335
00:13:55,568 --> 00:13:56,668
I'll go first and help you.

336
00:13:58,008 --> 00:14:00,568
(With You Seok's help)

337
00:14:01,278 --> 00:14:02,337
Okay.

338
00:14:02,338 --> 00:14:04,454
(She gets on a fishing boat for the first time in her life.)

339
00:14:04,478 --> 00:14:06,008
Okay. Hello.

340
00:14:06,678 --> 00:14:07,717
Hello.

341
00:14:07,718 --> 00:14:10,348
(An Youn Suk, Lady of the gizzard shad boat)

342
00:14:11,388 --> 00:14:12,517
Let's go fishing.

343
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:14,858
Okay. Fish.

344
00:14:15,758 --> 00:14:16,838
You said it so secretively.

345
00:14:17,218 --> 00:14:19,357
We have to go about 20 minutes.

346
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:21,498
Okay. Got it.

347
00:14:22,258 --> 00:14:23,657
I've never been on something like this.

348
00:14:23,658 --> 00:14:26,328
(Crossing the dark ocean to go to the fishery)

349
00:14:26,698 --> 00:14:28,238
The nighttime boat ride...

350
00:14:29,168 --> 00:14:30,268
is so dark.

351
00:14:30,538 --> 00:14:33,307
- You really can't see anything. - Oh, my.

352
00:14:33,308 --> 00:14:34,478
(In the pitch-black darkness)

353
00:14:36,378 --> 00:14:38,177
- It's really pitch-black darkness. - It is.

354
00:14:38,178 --> 00:14:39,778
(Only their boat is going out into sea.)

355
00:14:40,008 --> 00:14:43,617
I'm sure it won't be like this when we're catching gizzard shad,

356
00:14:43,618 --> 00:14:45,587
- but isn't it romantic right now? - It's really nice now.

357
00:14:45,588 --> 00:14:47,858
Oh, my. Look at the moon!

358
00:14:50,518 --> 00:14:52,787
- The moon is so bright. - Oh, my.

359
00:14:52,788 --> 00:14:53,857
(The bright moon shining all alone)

360
00:14:53,858 --> 00:14:56,598
This feels so great, doesn't it?

361
00:14:57,558 --> 00:14:59,667
The mood is so nice.

362
00:14:59,668 --> 00:15:02,798
- It's so nice. - It's so nice and cool.

363
00:15:03,398 --> 00:15:05,137
I love the lights in the distance.

364
00:15:05,138 --> 00:15:06,768
And we're on the water.

365
00:15:07,308 --> 00:15:08,308
It's so romantic, right?

366
00:15:08,308 --> 00:15:09,308
It's nice and cool, right?

367
00:15:09,309 --> 00:15:10,507
(The Yeosu night sea is full of romance.)

368
00:15:10,508 --> 00:15:12,477
We're out in the sea when the moon is still up.

369
00:15:12,478 --> 00:15:15,518
(What a unique experience to have before work.)

370
00:15:16,448 --> 00:15:19,287
The breeze feels so good.

371
00:15:19,288 --> 00:15:20,418
The breeze is amazing.

372
00:15:22,158 --> 00:15:24,157
(It's been 10 minutes since they set sail.)

373
00:15:24,158 --> 00:15:26,788
I'm feeling queasy. Does it mean I'm getting seasickness?

374
00:15:28,028 --> 00:15:31,098
(Seasickness kicks in as she's soaking up the romance.)

375
00:15:31,468 --> 00:15:33,227
It must be that my heart is pounding...

376
00:15:33,228 --> 00:15:35,337
- because I'm so excited. - Because you're so excited.

377
00:15:35,338 --> 00:15:37,938
(She tries to deny the seasickness with her positive energy.)

378
00:15:39,238 --> 00:15:43,138
(But the seasickness has already kicked in.)

379
00:15:43,408 --> 00:15:45,408
Sun Young, you need to look out into the distance.

380
00:15:46,378 --> 00:15:47,658
I'll look out into the distance.

381
00:15:49,948 --> 00:15:53,348
(But there's nothing out there for her to look at.)

382
00:15:54,858 --> 00:15:59,988
(I will get through it and push forward)

383
00:16:00,828 --> 00:16:03,198
(How Sun Young Fights off Seasickness: 1. Singing)

384
00:16:03,758 --> 00:16:06,698
(Sun Young is so cute.)

385
00:16:07,368 --> 00:16:09,038
Hello, dear viewers.

386
00:16:09,798 --> 00:16:11,608
We're out on the Yeosu sea...

387
00:16:12,668 --> 00:16:14,207
to catch gizzard shad.

388
00:16:14,208 --> 00:16:15,677
(Whom is she talking to?)

389
00:16:15,678 --> 00:16:16,778
I'm fine.

390
00:16:17,678 --> 00:16:20,548
This seasickness is psychological.

391
00:16:21,748 --> 00:16:22,848
I'm fine.

392
00:16:23,448 --> 00:16:24,448
It's okay.

393
00:16:25,448 --> 00:16:27,547
Once my dopamine hits the roof, the seasickness will be gone.

394
00:16:27,548 --> 00:16:29,217
You're right. It'll be gone once we start working.

395
00:16:29,218 --> 00:16:30,518
I'm a dopamine addict.

396
00:16:32,358 --> 00:16:34,674
(Waiting for that dopamine rush, they sail on for 20 more minutes.)

397
00:16:34,698 --> 00:16:36,178
- Are we here? - It's not hot at all.

398
00:16:36,358 --> 00:16:37,897
- Yes, we're here. - Right. It's refreshing and nice.

399
00:16:37,898 --> 00:16:39,604
(They've already arrived at the fishing spot.)

400
00:16:39,628 --> 00:16:40,728
I should prepare this.

401
00:16:42,238 --> 00:16:43,238
What is that?

402
00:16:43,239 --> 00:16:46,438
(The lady prepares something.)

403
00:16:47,638 --> 00:16:50,507
(Is she casting the net right here and now?)

404
00:16:50,508 --> 00:16:53,077
Is the net coming up with fish right away?

405
00:16:53,078 --> 00:16:54,307
- Yes. - Right now?

406
00:16:54,308 --> 00:16:56,947
We'll wait for about 20 minutes after casting the net,

407
00:16:56,948 --> 00:16:58,287
- Yes. - and then we'll haul it back up.

408
00:16:58,288 --> 00:16:59,648
Oh, I see.

409
00:17:00,288 --> 00:17:02,458
(Today's gizzard shad fishing method)

410
00:17:02,818 --> 00:17:06,158
(Drift gill net)

411
00:17:06,528 --> 00:17:11,598
(Reading the tide and the gizzard shad's path, )

412
00:17:11,868 --> 00:17:16,338
(you let the net drift with the current.)

413
00:17:16,668 --> 00:17:18,337
(A school of gizzard shad gets trapped...)

414
00:17:18,338 --> 00:17:21,908
(as they swim past the net!)

415
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:26,248
(Since gizzard shad are highly sensitive and easily stressed, )

416
00:17:27,748 --> 00:17:30,678
(you need to haul the net back up right after a 20-minute wait.)

417
00:17:32,018 --> 00:17:34,617
(After that, you just have to get the fish off the net!)

418
00:17:34,618 --> 00:17:37,788
(This is what the siblings should do today!)

419
00:17:38,358 --> 00:17:40,357
So, we throw the net and pull it right back up.

420
00:17:40,358 --> 00:17:42,334
(The lady will be handling the net to ensure everyone's safety.)

421
00:17:42,358 --> 00:17:44,967
This is fascinating. I've never seen a fishing net cast like this before.

422
00:17:44,968 --> 00:17:46,598
(They're casting 2 nets today!)

423
00:17:47,198 --> 00:17:48,198
Done.

424
00:17:49,368 --> 00:17:50,398
It's done.

425
00:17:51,338 --> 00:17:54,338
- We'll pull it up 20 minutes later. - I see.

426
00:17:54,738 --> 00:17:57,078
What do we do for the next 20 minutes?

427
00:17:57,638 --> 00:17:59,248
- Should we just wait? - Yes.

428
00:17:59,948 --> 00:18:02,447
- We just leave it in the water... - Yes.

429
00:18:02,448 --> 00:18:05,317
For about 20 minutes and pull it back up. That's all.

430
00:18:05,318 --> 00:18:06,994
(Waiting is the key to catching gizzard shad.)

431
00:18:07,018 --> 00:18:09,157
- Are you up? - Good morning.

432
00:18:09,158 --> 00:18:11,427
- I'll go wash up really quickly. - Okay.

433
00:18:11,428 --> 00:18:14,187
I have to take my medicine too.

434
00:18:14,188 --> 00:18:15,727
(It's 3:40am. Team Land is busy getting ready to go out.)

435
00:18:15,728 --> 00:18:19,668
I wonder if Sun Young and You Seok are doing okay out there at sea.

436
00:18:20,598 --> 00:18:24,168
(Sang Hun comes out first after finishing getting ready.)

437
00:18:24,298 --> 00:18:26,607
This is nice. It's really nice to work in this weather.

438
00:18:26,608 --> 00:18:27,837
(It's so cool early in the morning, which makes it way easier to work.)

439
00:18:27,838 --> 00:18:28,978
Let's get going.

440
00:18:29,238 --> 00:18:30,378
What's that?

441
00:18:31,278 --> 00:18:32,607
It's only 4am now. I've never worked...

442
00:18:32,608 --> 00:18:33,608
(Yoon Seo has never worked early in the morning before.)

443
00:18:33,609 --> 00:18:35,148
this early in the morning before.

444
00:18:35,548 --> 00:18:37,847
- Working early is better in summer. - That's right.

445
00:18:37,848 --> 00:18:40,047
We got an early start when we went out to the sea, right?

446
00:18:40,048 --> 00:18:41,734
(Avoiding the peak heat hours is a smart move in midsummer.)

447
00:18:41,758 --> 00:18:43,017
(Glancing)

448
00:18:43,018 --> 00:18:45,527
You must've felt different yesterday morning...

449
00:18:45,528 --> 00:18:48,958
while waiting to prank us. How do you feel now?

450
00:18:49,528 --> 00:18:50,568
How do you feel, Sang Hun?

451
00:18:50,958 --> 00:18:52,027
(Hissing and sighing)

452
00:18:52,028 --> 00:18:54,868
- Like I've been taken for a ride. - Like you've been taken for a ride?

453
00:18:54,898 --> 00:18:57,338
- I feel like a fish in a fish trap. - A fish in a fish trap.

454
00:18:57,568 --> 00:18:59,037
When you were waiting for us in that wig yesterday,

455
00:18:59,038 --> 00:19:00,837
- you never imagined this, right? - I was excited. Absolutely.

456
00:19:00,838 --> 00:19:01,838
(He couldn't even imagine this situation.)

457
00:19:01,839 --> 00:19:03,337
Everything on this show is real.

458
00:19:03,338 --> 00:19:04,877
You guys don't even have time to take a break.

459
00:19:04,878 --> 00:19:06,378
Of course. We do everything here.

460
00:19:06,748 --> 00:19:08,648
We'll become rich if we keep living like this.

461
00:19:10,418 --> 00:19:12,248
We're going to become rich.

462
00:19:13,048 --> 00:19:14,388
- Hello? - You Seok?

463
00:19:15,018 --> 00:19:16,087
Can't you hear me?

464
00:19:16,088 --> 00:19:17,717
- I can hear you clearly. Go on. - You know...

465
00:19:17,718 --> 00:19:21,527
- Since we're out at sea, - Yes.

466
00:19:21,528 --> 00:19:22,857
Our reception might be a bit spotty.

467
00:19:22,858 --> 00:19:24,968
Right. Isn't it nice to be out at sea?

468
00:19:25,668 --> 00:19:27,128
It's so cool here.

469
00:19:27,368 --> 00:19:28,368
(Relieved)

470
00:19:28,369 --> 00:19:29,974
- There's a nice breeze blowing. - I see.

471
00:19:29,998 --> 00:19:31,197
- You're jealous, aren't you? - Are you okay?

472
00:19:31,198 --> 00:19:32,207
Sorry?

473
00:19:32,208 --> 00:19:33,867
You're jealous that we're out at sea, aren't you?

474
00:19:33,868 --> 00:19:35,637
No. I've been out at sea many times before.

475
00:19:35,638 --> 00:19:36,638
So I'm not jealous.

476
00:19:37,538 --> 00:19:39,477
By the way, you sound pretty excited.

477
00:19:39,478 --> 00:19:41,448
Did your inner boat captain alter ego come out?

478
00:19:41,778 --> 00:19:44,448
Well, the whole sea is mine, you know.

479
00:19:47,148 --> 00:19:49,518
Is Sun Young doing okay? I bet she barely got any sleep.

480
00:19:49,958 --> 00:19:51,457
She's getting seasickness.

481
00:19:51,458 --> 00:19:53,357
- Oh, no. - I'm worried about her.

482
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:55,957
Jung Ah, I couldn't feel any better.

483
00:19:55,958 --> 00:19:56,997
Oh, I get it.

484
00:19:56,998 --> 00:19:59,527
I've never been better over the last four months.

485
00:19:59,528 --> 00:20:00,667
Oh, really?

486
00:20:00,668 --> 00:20:02,337
You'd be surprised.

487
00:20:02,338 --> 00:20:04,098
I guess you're in the worst shape right now.

488
00:20:04,168 --> 00:20:05,568
Like I said, I'm in the best shape.

489
00:20:05,938 --> 00:20:07,037
- But you're getting seasickness. - Your bucket list...

490
00:20:07,038 --> 00:20:08,118
This was on my bucket list.

491
00:20:08,978 --> 00:20:10,437
Mentioning her bucket list is the sign that she's not okay.

492
00:20:10,438 --> 00:20:11,678
Right. She's not okay.

493
00:20:12,108 --> 00:20:15,348
- See you later, Jung Ah. - See you after work.

494
00:20:15,618 --> 00:20:16,777
Okay. Go for it.

495
00:20:16,778 --> 00:20:18,018
- Go for it. - Go for it.

496
00:20:20,418 --> 00:20:21,487
(Thinking hard)

497
00:20:21,488 --> 00:20:22,618
Wait. Think about it.

498
00:20:22,988 --> 00:20:25,288
They left home at 3am, right?

499
00:20:26,088 --> 00:20:28,928
Have they gotten there? Are they on the boat right now?

500
00:20:29,128 --> 00:20:31,727
But I didn't hear any wind over the phone. Did you?

501
00:20:31,728 --> 00:20:32,728
No.

502
00:20:32,729 --> 00:20:34,297
- If they were sailing... - Right?

503
00:20:34,298 --> 00:20:36,568
Right. I don't think they're on a boat.

504
00:20:36,938 --> 00:20:38,637
- A boat? - I don't think they're on a boat.

505
00:20:38,638 --> 00:20:40,768
I think they were lying.

506
00:20:41,008 --> 00:20:42,608
That would be the biggest twist ever.

507
00:20:43,138 --> 00:20:44,408
So they're acting right now?

508
00:20:44,778 --> 00:20:46,677
- Right. I think... - I think she was lying...

509
00:20:46,678 --> 00:20:48,647
- about her seasickness too. - I think that was a lie too.

510
00:20:48,648 --> 00:20:50,717
- Oh, I think... - I didn't hear any wind.

511
00:20:50,718 --> 00:20:52,094
(They're completely doubting the other team.)

512
00:20:52,118 --> 00:20:55,057
He talked about how the reception was bad because they were on a boat,

513
00:20:55,058 --> 00:20:56,717
- but that was totally unnecessary. - Right.

514
00:20:56,718 --> 00:20:59,027
- Our reception might be spotty. - You're right.

515
00:20:59,028 --> 00:21:00,028
(He was just too kind.)

516
00:21:00,028 --> 00:21:01,028
What do you think?

517
00:21:01,458 --> 00:21:02,527
- You know everything, don't you? - We're right about that, aren't we?

518
00:21:02,528 --> 00:21:03,758
- Tell us. - I...

519
00:21:04,028 --> 00:21:06,309
- Make a video call to them. - Make a video call to them.

