00:31:22,378 --> 00:31:24,418
- The eel made a hole through this. - Are you okay?

777
00:31:24,678 --> 00:31:26,047
- It must be no joke. - Oh, we got a hairtail.

778
00:31:26,048 --> 00:31:28,217
(They also caught...)

779
00:31:28,218 --> 00:31:29,718
- Awesome. It's a hairtail. - Nice.

780
00:31:30,018 --> 00:31:32,428
- All right. - Look at its teeth.

781
00:31:32,628 --> 00:31:33,788
What kind of fish is this?

782
00:31:34,388 --> 00:31:36,028
Red barracuda. You can make stew with it.

783
00:31:37,158 --> 00:31:41,628
(They continue the dynamic gizzard shad harvest.)

784
00:31:41,998 --> 00:31:43,038
(Cheering with joy)

785
00:31:44,768 --> 00:31:46,467
Yes, I'll make sure not to damage the gills.

786
00:31:46,468 --> 00:31:47,607
(Her dopamine level has maxed out.)

787
00:31:47,608 --> 00:31:48,808
I'll make sure they don't die.

788
00:31:49,408 --> 00:31:52,038
(As they collect gizzard shad non-stop...)

789
00:31:52,578 --> 00:31:54,347
(It's already 5am now.)

790
00:31:54,348 --> 00:31:57,048
(90 minutes have passed.)

791
00:31:58,118 --> 00:31:59,387
We're here.

792
00:31:59,388 --> 00:32:01,628
(They've finally finished untangling fish from one net.)

793
00:32:01,948 --> 00:32:04,288
(A round of applause for our amazing hard work)

794
00:32:05,288 --> 00:32:08,658
(They look inside the tank for an interim check.)

795
00:32:08,798 --> 00:32:11,158
I didn't know how hard it was to catch gizzard shad.

796
00:32:12,058 --> 00:32:14,697
I thought we had caught a mountain of gizzard shad.

797
00:32:14,698 --> 00:32:15,898
- Right. - Right.

798
00:32:16,268 --> 00:32:18,168
But we caught way less than I thought.

799
00:32:18,638 --> 00:32:20,237
Right. That's why people say gizzard shad are hard to get.

800
00:32:20,238 --> 00:32:21,608
Oh, my. That's beautiful.

801
00:32:22,508 --> 00:32:25,478
(Something blew Sun Young's mind.)

802
00:32:26,008 --> 00:32:27,947
(As if to prove the hours of their hard work...)

803
00:32:27,948 --> 00:32:29,148
The sun is coming up.

804
00:32:29,878 --> 00:32:31,218
That's magnificent.

805
00:32:32,318 --> 00:32:34,117
We were too busy working to realize the sun was coming up.

806
00:32:34,118 --> 00:32:36,658
(the sun peeks through.)

807
00:32:40,258 --> 00:32:41,428
My, that's so beautiful.

808
00:32:44,658 --> 00:32:47,797
(As night meets morning...)

809
00:32:47,798 --> 00:32:49,238
It's not hot at all, right?

810
00:32:49,368 --> 00:32:50,897
- The weather is great. - It's so great.

811
00:32:50,898 --> 00:32:52,858
(The siblings' gizzard shad boat sails smoothly.)

812
00:32:53,008 --> 00:32:54,867
It's so beautiful with the sun coming up.

813
00:32:54,868 --> 00:32:56,137
(Their hearts are filled with lingering emotions.)

814
00:32:56,138 --> 00:32:57,538
Seriously...

815
00:32:58,078 --> 00:33:00,978
I feel perfectly fine now that I'm working.

816
00:33:01,278 --> 00:33:03,948
I feel a little queasy when I stay still.

817
00:33:04,478 --> 00:33:05,688
Right. I guess so.

818
00:33:06,188 --> 00:33:07,748
That means you're built for hard labor.

819
00:33:08,118 --> 00:33:09,118
- Sorry? - You're built for hard labor.

820
00:33:09,119 --> 00:33:11,057
- I'm built for the dopamine rush. - You're built for hard labor.

821
00:33:11,058 --> 00:33:12,698
(She's just built for the dopamine rush.)

822
00:33:13,628 --> 00:33:17,198
(Meanwhile, the captain's wife is preparing the next dopamine rush.)

823
00:33:17,528 --> 00:33:18,528
Oh, right. We have to wait again...

824
00:33:18,529 --> 00:33:20,228
- after casting the net. - That's right.

825
00:33:20,698 --> 00:33:21,867
- We have to wait again. - We have to do it all over again.

826
00:33:21,868 --> 00:33:22,897
Yes. Got it.

827
00:33:22,898 --> 00:33:25,378
(They will haul up the net for the 2nd time 20 minutes later.)

828
00:33:26,108 --> 00:33:28,337
The sea is so beautiful.

829
00:33:28,338 --> 00:33:29,914
(What kind of dopamine rush will the second net bring?)

830
00:33:29,938 --> 00:33:32,418
(Meanwhile, the three of them are still on their way to work.)

831
00:33:32,508 --> 00:33:33,608
It's beautiful.

832
00:33:34,948 --> 00:33:36,677
I want to paint that scenery.

833
00:33:36,678 --> 00:33:37,818
It's amazing.

834
00:33:39,518 --> 00:33:41,888
- It could seem like the sunset. - That's right.

835
00:33:42,148 --> 00:33:43,757
And it could seem like the sunrise, depending on the point of view.

836
00:33:43,758 --> 00:33:44,887
(The beautiful scenery washes away their doubts.)

837
00:33:44,888 --> 00:33:46,128
I think we're almost there.

838
00:33:47,028 --> 00:33:49,598
Wait. Where are we? I see the sea and the mudflats.

839
00:33:50,928 --> 00:33:52,567
Why did we end up at the mudflats?

840
00:33:52,568 --> 00:33:53,867
(The mudflats stretch out endlessly outside the window?)

841
00:33:53,868 --> 00:33:54,898
The mudflats?

842
00:33:56,738 --> 00:33:57,838
Gosh, seriously.

843
00:33:58,068 --> 00:33:59,568
This is ridiculous.

844
00:34:01,008 --> 00:34:02,277
Maybe we'll be working at the mudflats.

845
00:34:02,278 --> 00:34:04,537
(The mudflats, not land?)

846
00:34:04,538 --> 00:34:05,608
The mudflats...

847
00:34:06,378 --> 00:34:08,808
- I think that's the case. - It's the mudflats.

848
00:34:10,778 --> 00:34:13,138
- I can't believe this. My gosh. - I think that's the case.

849
00:34:13,688 --> 00:34:15,148
I would rather go out to sea.

850
00:34:15,818 --> 00:34:18,218
Working in the mudflats is four times as hard.

851
00:34:18,888 --> 00:34:20,757
So, the mudflats is technically just a field?

852
00:34:20,758 --> 00:34:22,718
- I guess that's what they meant. - The mudflats.

853
00:34:23,758 --> 00:34:24,827
This is driving me crazy.

854
00:34:24,828 --> 00:34:25,967
(What kind of work will they do here?)

855
00:34:25,968 --> 00:34:27,448
- Shall we get out of the car? - Yes.

856
00:34:30,568 --> 00:34:31,738
(Sighing)

857
00:34:32,238 --> 00:34:35,538
(The vast mudflats stretch out right in front of them.)

858
00:34:35,808 --> 00:34:37,107
What are we going to do here?

859
00:34:37,108 --> 00:34:39,468
The tide is completely out. Should we go into the mudflats?

860
00:34:40,048 --> 00:34:41,448
I'm working in the mudflats again.

861
00:34:41,908 --> 00:34:43,828
They brought us here right when the tide is out.

862
00:34:45,118 --> 00:34:46,347
What can we harvest here?

863
00:34:46,348 --> 00:34:47,488
(What can we harvest here?)

864
00:34:47,948 --> 00:34:48,988
(Cheering half-heartedly)

865
00:34:49,258 --> 00:34:50,758
I'm at the mudflats.

866
00:34:51,058 --> 00:34:53,758
(She gave in.)

867
00:34:54,028 --> 00:34:55,264
Are we going into the mudflats?

868
00:34:55,288 --> 00:34:57,797
(Will they really be working in the mudflats?)

869
00:34:57,798 --> 00:34:59,604
We're not, right? We would've brought the shoes...

870
00:34:59,628 --> 00:35:01,667
- Oh, that way? - Hold on.

871
00:35:01,668 --> 00:35:03,838
- Gosh. They'll never tell us. - What?

872
00:35:04,038 --> 00:35:05,567
I keep getting fooled.

873
00:35:05,568 --> 00:35:06,667
I've been completely fooled.

874
00:35:06,668 --> 00:35:09,278
(We, the production team, had no intention of tricking you.)

875
00:35:10,178 --> 00:35:11,677
Is there something to harvest here?

876
00:35:11,678 --> 00:35:13,358
(They leave the mudflats and head inland.)

877
00:35:15,918 --> 00:35:16,978
Greenhouses.

878
00:35:17,218 --> 00:35:19,688
- Greenhouses. - What did you say about them?

879
00:35:20,288 --> 00:35:22,048
- Cucumbers. No. - Cucumbers?

880
00:35:22,248 --> 00:35:23,487
- Zucchini. - Zucchini?

881
00:35:23,488 --> 00:35:24,888
(In a field lined with greenhouses)

882
00:35:25,258 --> 00:35:26,628
What a strong smell.

883
00:35:28,228 --> 00:35:29,327
- How pretty. - It smells nice.

884
00:35:29,328 --> 00:35:30,957
(A crop that smells amazing?)

885
00:35:30,958 --> 00:35:32,967
- Gosh, the smell is... - It smells really nice.

886
00:35:32,968 --> 00:35:35,097
- Right? - Seriously, the smell is...

887
00:35:35,098 --> 00:35:36,578
(What kind of labor awaits the trio?)

888
00:35:39,108 --> 00:35:41,908
- Figs. Isn't it the scent of figs? - Yes, it's the scent of figs.

889
00:35:42,038 --> 00:35:43,584
- It must be the scent of figs. - Right?

890
00:35:43,608 --> 00:35:44,937
- Figs. - They are figs.

891
00:35:44,938 --> 00:35:46,078
- My gosh. - Are they ripe?

892
00:35:46,748 --> 00:35:48,807
- I have a feeling it's figs. - It's figs.

893
00:35:48,808 --> 00:35:50,008
(The answer is fragrant figs.)

894
00:35:50,648 --> 00:35:51,968
Today's labor is harvesting figs,

895
00:35:52,148 --> 00:35:54,447
a Yeosu specialty grown with plenty of sunshine...

896
00:35:54,448 --> 00:35:56,187
and in a mild climate.

897
00:35:56,188 --> 00:35:58,988
(Yeosu's specialty, figs)

898
00:35:59,658 --> 00:36:01,958
(Said to have been enjoyed even by Cleopatra)

899
00:36:02,828 --> 00:36:05,198
(The mysterious fruit, fig)

900
00:36:05,798 --> 00:36:07,698
(Muhwa, Korean for fig, means flowerless.)

901
00:36:07,968 --> 00:36:10,397
Compared to other fruits, there's little to waste.

902
00:36:10,398 --> 00:36:11,467
(Unlike other fruits that develop after the flowers fall)

903
00:36:11,468 --> 00:36:12,468
It's easy to eat.

904
00:36:12,468 --> 00:36:13,468
(The fig itself is a flower.)

905
00:36:13,469 --> 00:36:16,208
(Flowers blooming inside)

906
00:36:16,608 --> 00:36:19,708
Diabetics aren't supposed to have sweet food.

907
00:36:20,208 --> 00:36:21,848
But figs help lower blood sugar levels.

908
00:36:22,378 --> 00:36:24,348
Many come to Yeosu to buy figs.

909
00:36:24,518 --> 00:36:27,188
Our figs are high in quality and sweet.

910
00:36:27,748 --> 00:36:31,188
The land gets plenty of sunlight, making it ideal for growing figs.

911
00:36:31,718 --> 00:36:34,158
The sea breeze helps make...

912
00:36:34,788 --> 00:36:35,827
the figs sweeter.

913
00:36:35,828 --> 00:36:37,197
(Known for their deep, rich sweetness)

914
00:36:37,198 --> 00:36:38,198
The figs are very tasty.

915
00:36:38,199 --> 00:36:39,928
(Known for their deep, rich sweetness)

916
00:36:41,028 --> 00:36:45,738
(Shall we go pick some sweet flowers now?)

917
00:36:46,168 --> 00:36:48,167
- Hi. - Hi.

918
00:36:48,168 --> 00:36:49,177
Hi.

919
00:36:49,178 --> 00:36:51,208
(Kang Jeong Ja)

920
00:36:51,408 --> 00:36:55,408
You have to harvest only the ripe figs.

921
00:36:55,878 --> 00:36:56,878
Like this one.

922
00:36:57,778 --> 00:37:00,017
There are ripe ones over here.

923
00:37:00,018 --> 00:37:01,348
These are green, right?

924
00:37:01,748 --> 00:37:05,488
Only harvest the red ones. They're soft when you touch them.

925
00:37:06,028 --> 00:37:08,288
You'll be able to spot the red ones.

926
00:37:08,488 --> 00:37:09,998
- Red ones? - Yes.

927
00:37:11,198 --> 00:37:13,827
When you touch them, you'll feel the difference.

928
00:37:13,828 --> 00:37:15,327
The bottom of the figs is split open.

929
00:37:15,328 --> 00:37:16,397
(Even if it's green, )

930
00:37:16,398 --> 00:37:18,574
(if it's soft or the bottom is split, the fig is ripe.)

931
00:37:18,598 --> 00:37:19,608
How do we harvest them?

932
00:37:20,768 --> 00:37:22,837
- Grab one like so. - Okay.

933
00:37:22,838 --> 00:37:25,577
- Do we push it with our thumbs? - Yes, don't crush the fruit.

934
00:37:25,578 --> 00:37:27,977
Grab it around here and push it down.

935
00:37:27,978 --> 00:37:29,447
- Okay. - Like so.

936
00:37:29,448 --> 00:37:32,278
- Got it. We use our thumbs. - Yes, use your thumb.

937
00:37:33,218 --> 00:37:34,847
- It's easy to pick. - Yes.

938
00:37:34,848 --> 00:37:37,858
- The figs are easy to pick. - Okay.

939
00:37:38,118 --> 00:37:39,457
- Like this. - They're delivered...

940
00:37:39,458 --> 00:37:40,828
straight to the customers.

941
00:37:41,388 --> 00:37:43,397
- All right? - Yes.

942
00:37:43,398 --> 00:37:44,398
Thank you.

943
00:37:45,498 --> 00:37:46,528
Let's get started.

944
00:37:46,828 --> 00:37:49,028
Figs

945
00:37:49,938 --> 00:37:50,967
Enter.

946
00:37:50,968 --> 00:37:52,438
(The players enter.)

947
00:37:54,408 --> 00:37:55,408
My gosh!

948
00:37:56,538 --> 00:37:57,578
I see plenty here.

949
00:37:58,508 --> 00:38:00,808
(Yoon Seo strikes gold from the start.)

950
00:38:01,178 --> 00:38:02,178
(Snap)

951
00:38:02,878 --> 00:38:03,878
(Snap)

952
00:38:05,618 --> 00:38:08,488
(Jung Ah also found figs.)

953
00:38:09,158 --> 00:38:10,218
(Snap)

954
00:38:11,658 --> 00:38:14,788
(She snaps the figs off the stems as taught.)

955
00:38:15,188 --> 00:38:16,628
The ripe ones snap off easily.

956
00:38:17,558 --> 00:38:19,468
- Ripe figs are easy to snap off. - Right?

957
00:38:20,828 --> 00:38:22,698
My gosh, this one's completely ripe. Look.

958
00:38:23,598 --> 00:38:25,167
The figs are easy to harvest.

959
00:38:25,168 --> 00:38:26,488
(Fig picking is relatively easy.)

960
00:38:26,638 --> 00:38:30,107
The work isn't too hard because the sun isn't out yet this morning.

961
00:38:30,108 --> 00:38:31,548
(Perfect conditions with no sun yet)

962
00:38:31,578 --> 00:38:33,777
There's a reason farmers get up early in the morning.

963
00:38:33,778 --> 00:38:35,778
(Early mornings are a must when farming.)

964
00:38:36,778 --> 00:38:40,248
(Even the locals work at 5am or 5pm, when the sun is less intense.)

965
00:38:42,888 --> 00:38:45,018
The scent of figs is just amazing.

966
00:38:45,558 --> 00:38:46,628
I know, right?

967
00:38:47,128 --> 00:38:49,327
I've gotten used to the scent already.

968
00:38:49,328 --> 00:38:51,648
(The lovely fragrance makes the job even more satisfying.)

969
00:38:52,998 --> 00:38:53,998
(In awe)

970
00:38:54,768 --> 00:38:57,198
The scent is beyond simply nice.

971
00:38:59,468 --> 00:39:00,538
(Amazed)

972
00:39:02,408 --> 00:39:04,238
The figs have a strong scent, don't they?

973
00:39:04,438 --> 00:39:05,907
Yes, have figs always had such a rich scent?

974
00:39:05,908 --> 00:39:07,424
(The sweet fig fragrance keeps their spirits up.)

975
00:39:07,448 --> 00:39:09,148
Seriously, I'm telling you.

976
00:39:10,048 --> 00:39:12,048
Figs from Yeosu are a must-try.

977
00:39:13,418 --> 00:39:16,418
- The fruits are huge. - Yes, they're plump.

978
00:39:17,118 --> 00:39:19,558
There's something about the way a fig feels when you hold it.

979
00:39:20,888 --> 00:39:23,198
It's different. The fig feels different.

980
00:39:24,958 --> 00:39:27,528
What's with this crab? Look at the crab.

981
00:39:27,968 --> 00:39:29,028
What's with it?

982
00:39:29,968 --> 00:39:32,608
(Yeosu figs are no joke!)

983
00:39:32,738 --> 00:39:33,808
(Impressed)

984
00:39:34,038 --> 00:39:35,207
I'm loving the scent.

985
00:39:35,208 --> 00:39:36,937
(Picking them firsthand reveals...)

986
00:39:36,938 --> 00:39:38,738
(just how plump and fragrant Yeosu figs are.)

987
00:39:39,808 --> 00:39:40,808
These guys.

988
00:39:40,809 --> 00:39:42,178
(Fig guys)

989
00:39:43,018 --> 00:39:45,048
Gosh, here they are.

990
00:39:49,958 --> 00:39:50,958
One.

991
00:39:52,358 --> 00:39:53,358
Two.

992
00:39:56,028 --> 00:39:57,028
Two figs.

993
00:39:58,728 --> 00:39:59,768
Together,

994
00:40:01,298 --> 00:40:02,398
they make a heart.

995
00:40:03,298 --> 00:40:04,298
Here.

996
00:40:05,298 --> 00:40:06,308
A fig...

997
00:40:06,938 --> 00:40:07,938
heart.

998
00:40:07,939 --> 00:40:08,944
(Fig promotion that might backfire)

999
00:40:08,968 --> 00:40:11,338
(Reality hits.)

1000
00:40:11,638 --> 00:40:12,708
(Snap)

1001
00:40:13,278 --> 00:40:14,278
(Snap)

1002
00:40:16,478 --> 00:40:17,478
I'm rich.

1003
00:40:18,578 --> 00:40:21,588
(Filling the basket with figs in high spirits)

1004
00:40:22,148 --> 00:40:24,718
(Groaning)

1005
00:40:25,288 --> 00:40:28,288
(The basket has gotten heavy.)

1006
00:40:28,858 --> 00:40:29,858
It's heavy.

1007
00:40:31,998 --> 00:40:35,368
(The harvest is going smoothly thanks to the ripe figs.)

1008
00:40:37,068 --> 00:40:38,138
Twist them gently.

1009
00:40:39,308 --> 00:40:42,138
Let's make sure I only pick the best ones.

1010
00:40:43,408 --> 00:40:44,478
Basket.

1011
00:40:46,148 --> 00:40:47,708
Hold on.

1012
00:40:48,348 --> 00:40:49,377
(In a mess)

1013
00:40:49,378 --> 00:40:50,448
Wait.

1014
00:40:51,818 --> 00:40:54,648
I'm literally passing through a jungle.

1015
00:40:55,748 --> 00:40:56,858
My gosh, already?

1016
00:40:58,058 --> 00:40:59,588
You work fast.

1017
00:41:00,158 --> 00:41:01,427
Is she trying to finish early?

1018
00:41:01,428 --> 00:41:04,028
(Harvesting figs at full speed)

1019
00:41:04,798 --> 00:41:07,398
I only picked the ones with high market value.

1020
00:41:07,598 --> 00:41:09,038
(Sang Hun has also filled a basket.)

1021
00:41:09,198 --> 00:41:11,437
Just look at them. Look at how they've split open.

1022
00:41:11,438 --> 00:41:14,008
(Everyone has filled one basket each.)

1023
00:41:15,708 --> 00:41:17,237
(Current time: 6am)

1024
00:41:17,238 --> 00:41:18,838
(Half an hour of harvesting has passed.)

1025
00:41:20,508 --> 00:41:23,678
(Just when everything seemed to be going smoothly)

1026
00:41:24,948 --> 00:41:25,988
(Groaning)

1027
00:41:26,088 --> 00:41:28,088
(Their backs are starting to ache.)

1028
00:41:28,518 --> 00:41:30,488
- The ripe ones are at the bottom. - Yes.

1029
00:41:31,458 --> 00:41:32,687
The colors are totally different.

1030
00:41:32,688 --> 00:41:35,328
(The problem is that the ripe figs are clustered near the bottom.)

1031
00:41:36,758 --> 00:41:37,797
(Sighing)

1032
00:41:37,798 --> 00:41:39,798
(Their lower backs are constantly being strained.)

1033
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:41,568
Oh, no.

1034
00:41:42,398 --> 00:41:44,868
- Oh, no. - It's...

1035
00:41:46,738 --> 00:41:48,437
Goodness. Here.

1036
00:41:48,438 --> 00:41:50,198
(A rather uncomfortable harvesting position)

1037
00:41:50,438 --> 00:41:53,778
This is one of the most uncomfortable positions,

1038
00:41:54,208 --> 00:41:56,018
maybe because it's so early.

1039
00:41:57,778 --> 00:42:00,418
This position might make me need to use the bathroom soon.

1040
00:42:01,488 --> 00:42:05,318
(The position definitely feels relieving, though.)

1041
00:42:08,088 --> 00:42:11,158
(Slowly running out of energy)

1042
00:42:11,798 --> 00:42:13,727
It gets hot even in the morning.

1043
00:42:13,728 --> 00:42:15,698
(Groaning)

1044
00:42:16,238 --> 00:42:17,238
(Sighing)

1045
00:42:17,239 --> 00:42:20,238
(Sweating buckets even without the sun)

1046
00:42:22,978 --> 00:42:24,008
Oh, my.

1047
00:42:24,238 --> 00:42:26,248
(Meanwhile, a fig leaf has been acquired.)

1048
00:42:27,108 --> 00:42:28,547
- Sang Hun. - Yes?

1049
00:42:28,548 --> 00:42:30,018
Look, it's a fan.

1050
00:42:30,778 --> 00:42:32,717
I'm using a fallen leaf as a fan.

1051
00:42:32,718 --> 00:42:34,018
(Introducing the leaf fan)

1052
00:42:34,518 --> 00:42:35,588
It feels nice.

1053
00:42:36,858 --> 00:42:39,258
(Smiling brightly, no matter how hard it gets)

1054
00:42:39,858 --> 00:42:43,258
(Positive Yoon Seo's way of coping)

1055
00:42:43,958 --> 00:42:46,198
I have to peek between the leaves.

1056
00:42:46,568 --> 00:42:48,368
Like, "Pardon me."

1057
00:42:49,898 --> 00:42:50,967
Here I go.

1058
00:42:50,968 --> 00:42:54,608
(Yoon Seo still inspects every fig carefully even when exhausted.)

1059
00:42:55,468 --> 00:42:58,108
(Working hard)

1060
00:42:58,708 --> 00:42:59,708
There aren't any here.

1061
00:43:02,448 --> 00:43:03,518
Oh, gosh.

1062
00:43:04,648 --> 00:43:05,718
It's empty.

1063
00:43:06,988 --> 00:43:08,217
Nice.

1064
00:43:08,218 --> 00:43:10,618
(Never losing her energy, even in the heat and exhaustion)

1065
00:43:11,588 --> 00:43:12,658
Pardon me.

1066
00:43:13,588 --> 00:43:14,827
I must've gotten it wrong.

1067
00:43:14,828 --> 00:43:16,028
(The seat cushion)

1068
00:43:16,398 --> 00:43:17,398
How do I wear it?

1069
00:43:18,228 --> 00:43:19,427
(Dancing)

1070
00:43:19,428 --> 00:43:20,627
- Is it like this? - No.

1071
00:43:20,628 --> 00:43:22,328
(Getting a little too hyper)

1072
00:43:23,068 --> 00:43:24,068
Really.

1073
00:43:25,768 --> 00:43:27,268
This one looks like a proper fig.

1074
00:43:28,238 --> 00:43:29,398
Did I just state the obvious?

1075
00:43:29,538 --> 00:43:32,108
(So hyper she's starting to lose her mind)

1076
00:43:37,693 --> 00:43:38,693
Really.

1077
00:43:40,433 --> 00:43:41,963
This one looks like a proper fig.

1078
00:43:42,863 --> 00:43:44,023
Did I just state the obvious?

1079
00:43:44,203 --> 00:43:46,773
(So hyper she's starting to lose her mind)

1080
00:43:51,773 --> 00:43:54,143
(Her upbeat mood leads to an impromptu fig promotion)

1081
00:43:58,543 --> 00:43:59,613
Fig.

1082
00:44:01,253 --> 00:44:03,453
(Dangerously charming)

1083
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:05,282
(Turning)

1084
00:44:05,283 --> 00:44:06,753
I so want to bite you.

1085
00:44:10,393 --> 00:44:12,463
Hurry up and work! What are you doing?

1086
00:44:13,433 --> 00:44:16,032
What is she doing in the middle of work?

1087
00:44:16,033 --> 00:44:17,103
Bite what?

1088
00:44:17,803 --> 00:44:18,803
(Laughing)

1089
00:44:18,804 --> 00:44:20,073
The ants might bite you.

1090
00:44:20,233 --> 00:44:22,973
(Unyielding)

1091
00:44:24,403 --> 00:44:25,672
It's heavy.

1092
00:44:25,673 --> 00:44:27,673
(Meanwhile, the workaholic Captain Yum...)

1093
00:44:28,273 --> 00:44:30,443
(squeezes into the narrow gap.)

1094
00:44:31,343 --> 00:44:33,253
(Snap)

1095
00:44:34,413 --> 00:44:36,183
(Spotted another fig)

1096
00:44:39,993 --> 00:44:43,323
(She continues to hunt for figs quietly.)

1097
00:44:44,823 --> 00:44:48,363
(Enter Yumdysseus)

1098
00:44:48,663 --> 00:44:50,463
(Walking)

1099
00:44:51,003 --> 00:44:52,802
(Looking around)

1100
00:44:52,803 --> 00:44:54,703
(Looking around)

1101
00:44:54,873 --> 00:44:56,073
(Snap)

1102
00:44:56,343 --> 00:44:57,403
(Snap)

1103
00:44:57,573 --> 00:44:59,543
(Snap)

1104
00:45:00,343 --> 00:45:03,183
(Just as the Greek army conquered Troy, )

1105
00:45:04,013 --> 00:45:09,013
(Yumdysseus is conquering the fig field.)

1106
00:45:09,653 --> 00:45:11,013
There are figs even way out there.

1107
00:45:12,053 --> 00:45:14,222
(Her troops are working just as hard.)

1108
00:45:14,223 --> 00:45:15,493
My goodness.

1109
00:45:16,663 --> 00:45:18,763
Oh, dear. I've harvested a lot.

1110
00:45:19,693 --> 00:45:21,063
- Did you? - Yes.

1111
00:45:21,963 --> 00:45:23,033
Take a look.

1112
00:45:23,663 --> 00:45:26,373
Hold on. Let me pick those figs.

1113
00:45:27,003 --> 00:45:28,403
I don't see any on this side.

1114
00:45:29,173 --> 00:45:30,742
I can tell at a glance.

1115
00:45:30,743 --> 00:45:32,219
(Did they clear the whole fig orchard in an hour?)

1116
00:45:32,243 --> 00:45:34,272
What now? The fig orchard ends here.

1117
00:45:34,273 --> 00:45:36,283
You've got to pick the ones in the greenhouses.

1118
00:45:36,743 --> 00:45:37,883
Are we done here?

1119
00:45:38,513 --> 00:45:39,613
Done, my foot.

1120
00:45:40,053 --> 00:45:43,023
We've got to harvest the figs in all the greenhouses, Sang Hun.

1121
00:45:43,753 --> 00:45:46,553
(They have to harvest the figs in the greenhouses.)

1122
00:45:47,153 --> 00:45:49,122
(The open-field orchard they just harvested)

1123
00:45:49,123 --> 00:45:52,593
(They still have the same amount of land left to harvest.)

1124
00:45:53,063 --> 00:45:55,693
Do the greenhouses also belong to them?

1125
00:45:56,663 --> 00:45:59,503
I thought the owners had a small plot of land.

1126
00:45:59,833 --> 00:46:02,632
- It was far from small. - It's a large-scale farm.

1127
00:46:02,633 --> 00:46:04,373
Jung Ah, are you in the first greenhouse?

1128
00:46:04,673 --> 00:46:06,772
Go to the next greenhouse.

1129
00:46:06,773 --> 00:46:08,643
The next one? The next greenhouse?

1130
00:46:10,683 --> 00:46:12,983
(And so, work begins inside the greenhouse.)

1131
00:46:13,653 --> 00:46:14,983
Hello, ma'am.

1132
00:46:17,123 --> 00:46:18,152
You have it tough.

1133
00:46:18,153 --> 00:46:20,893
Gosh, it's not tough.

1134
00:46:22,123 --> 00:46:23,662
Try one of the figs.

1135
00:46:23,663 --> 00:46:27,163
- May I? - Of course, try one.

1136
00:46:27,463 --> 00:46:28,492
Soft ones.

1137
00:46:28,493 --> 00:46:30,563
This one's soft. This fig feels soft.

1138
00:46:32,233 --> 00:46:33,233
Here.

1139
00:46:33,233 --> 00:46:34,233
(Excited)

1140
00:46:34,234 --> 00:46:35,533
Try one.

1141
00:46:37,073 --> 00:46:38,073
(In awe)

1142
00:46:39,203 --> 00:46:40,713
- Gosh, it's really good. - Right?

1143
00:46:41,973 --> 00:46:44,313
(His eyes widen.)

1144
00:46:45,083 --> 00:46:46,083
(In awe)

1145
00:46:46,084 --> 00:46:47,112
You've got to eat it whole.

1146
00:46:47,113 --> 00:46:48,553
(Is it that good?)

1147
00:46:49,453 --> 00:46:51,423
(Let's try it.)

1148
00:46:53,223 --> 00:46:54,922
The sweetness is on another level.

1149
00:46:54,923 --> 00:46:56,923
(Surprised)

1150
00:46:58,063 --> 00:46:59,693
- Were figs always this good? - Right?

1151
00:46:59,993 --> 00:47:01,262
Isn't it delicious?

1152
00:47:01,263 --> 00:47:02,763
I never knew figs tasted this good.

1153
00:47:03,103 --> 00:47:04,362
The sweetness is different.

1154
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:05,563
It's one that makes you happy.

1155
00:47:06,163 --> 00:47:07,333
Like a pear,

1156
00:47:07,773 --> 00:47:09,373
the fig isn't overwhelmingly sweet.

1157
00:47:09,943 --> 00:47:14,773
The sweetness gently spreads through your mouth.

1158
00:47:15,643 --> 00:47:17,712
- Right? It has a refined sweetness. - Yes.

1159
00:47:17,713 --> 00:47:19,243
The figs are just sweet enough.

1160
00:47:19,413 --> 00:47:22,113
Your entire mouth gets filled with the scent of figs.

1161
00:47:22,183 --> 00:47:23,883
My gosh, I'm so into figs now.

1162
00:47:25,223 --> 00:47:27,192
You should've tried one sooner.

1163
00:47:27,193 --> 00:47:28,893
(A taste you just can't resist)

1164
00:47:29,353 --> 00:47:30,792
Share these with the others.

1165
00:47:30,793 --> 00:47:32,493
- My gosh, it's so good. - Right?

1166
00:47:33,393 --> 00:47:34,393
(An endless supply)

1167
00:47:34,394 --> 00:47:36,033
- Oh, my goodness. - Try these too.

1168
00:47:37,033 --> 00:47:38,132
I had no idea.

1169
00:47:38,133 --> 00:47:41,073
(I had no idea how good figs were.)

1170
00:47:41,573 --> 00:47:43,172
Have them all. Pick some out to eat.

1171
00:47:43,173 --> 00:47:44,372
(After giving Sang Hun plenty of figs, )

1172
00:47:44,373 --> 00:47:45,603
(she casually walks away.)

1173
00:47:45,903 --> 00:47:47,872
- It's not overly sweet. - No.

1174
00:47:47,873 --> 00:47:49,433
- It's just sweet enough, right? - Yes.

1175
00:47:50,413 --> 00:47:51,683
The figs made me so happy.

1176
00:47:52,943 --> 00:47:54,012
(Amazed)

1177
00:47:54,013 --> 00:47:55,713
(Laughing)

1178
00:47:56,153 --> 00:47:58,953
(They are reenergized after eating some delicious figs!)

1179
00:47:59,523 --> 00:48:02,153
Have I ever worked this hard in my life?

1180
00:48:02,823 --> 00:48:04,343
If you work this hard, you'll make it.

1181
00:48:05,663 --> 00:48:08,063
If you succeed, you'll make it big.

1182
00:48:10,303 --> 00:48:11,303
(Working as hard as she possibly can)

1183
00:48:11,304 --> 00:48:12,333
Hold on.

1184
00:48:12,403 --> 00:48:14,533
(She thoroughly picks every last fig.)

1185
00:48:14,933 --> 00:48:16,573
I'm practically a hunter right now.

1186
00:48:17,273 --> 00:48:19,572
A hunter. I won't miss a single fig.

1187
00:48:19,573 --> 00:48:21,973
(The fig hunter leaves no fig behind.)

1188
00:48:24,683 --> 00:48:25,713
Give me a second.

1189
00:48:28,283 --> 00:48:30,623
(Suddenly plops down)

1190
00:48:32,283 --> 00:48:34,993
I get a completely different view when I lie down.

1191
00:48:36,123 --> 00:48:37,893
(Surprised)

1192
00:48:39,023 --> 00:48:40,303
Since I'm already on the ground.

1193
00:48:40,493 --> 00:48:43,403
(Picking figs is a piece of cake now.)

1194
00:48:44,003 --> 00:48:45,633
All done. This much should do.

1195
00:48:48,373 --> 00:48:52,543
(Everyone has fully gotten the hang of harvesting figs.)

1196
00:48:53,003 --> 00:48:54,042
Oh, my.

1197
00:48:54,043 --> 00:48:55,742
(Even the seemingly endless greenhouses are nearly finished.)

1198
00:48:55,743 --> 00:48:57,483
- I did that side. - What?

1199
00:48:58,883 --> 00:49:01,152
(They keep picking diligently...)

1200
00:49:01,153 --> 00:49:03,553
(until the very end.)

1201
00:49:03,783 --> 00:49:05,552
Are we done with the greenhouses?

1202
00:49:05,553 --> 00:49:07,193
You are. You picked everything here.

1203
00:49:08,023 --> 00:49:09,053
We're done.

1204
00:49:09,723 --> 00:49:12,593
(Current time: 7am, Fig harvesting complete)

1205
00:49:13,193 --> 00:49:14,962
We have to box them now.

1206
00:49:14,963 --> 00:49:18,333
(Shall we go pack them up now?)

1207
00:49:18,763 --> 00:49:20,102
Here they are.

1208
00:49:20,103 --> 00:49:21,903
(Meanwhile, Team Sea...)

1209
00:49:23,033 --> 00:49:25,543
(is working on the second net.)

1210
00:49:25,843 --> 00:49:27,742
Here they are!

1211
00:49:27,743 --> 00:49:29,882
(Now that they've got a feel for it, )

1212
00:49:29,883 --> 00:49:31,282
(their work speed picks up.)

1213
00:49:31,283 --> 00:49:33,383
I've gotten better at it.

1214
00:49:34,383 --> 00:49:35,383
Hairtail.

1215
00:49:35,384 --> 00:49:37,182
(You Seok can now...)

1216
00:49:37,183 --> 00:49:40,052
(handle a hairtail in one go.)

1217
00:49:40,053 --> 00:49:41,652
Fish are coming up.

1218
00:49:41,653 --> 00:49:42,723
Got it.

1219
00:49:44,063 --> 00:49:46,862
(Come, gizzard shad.)

1220
00:49:46,863 --> 00:49:49,163
(I'll get you all out of the net!)

1221
00:49:50,203 --> 00:49:53,203
(Almost a gizzard shad expert now)

1222
00:49:53,673 --> 00:49:54,673
Is it fun?

1223
00:49:54,674 --> 00:49:56,543
- Yes, it's fun. - You're good at it.

1224
00:49:57,243 --> 00:49:59,083
- Don't go to Seoul. Stay here. - You're good.

1225
00:49:59,203 --> 00:50:00,572
- Work here. - As long as...

1226
00:50:00,573 --> 00:50:01,742
you're willing to hire me.

1227
00:50:01,743 --> 00:50:02,743
(An offer to work on the gizzard shad fishing boat)

1228
00:50:02,744 --> 00:50:04,112
They told me to stay behind...

1229
00:50:04,113 --> 00:50:05,482
- Just stay here. - and...

1230
00:50:05,483 --> 00:50:07,053
- catch fish. - That's right.

1231
00:50:07,413 --> 00:50:08,613
- Should I? - Yes.

1232
00:50:08,853 --> 00:50:10,552
(The job offers keep coming.)

1233
00:50:10,553 --> 00:50:14,122
I should've become a fisherman or farmer instead of an actor.

1234
00:50:14,123 --> 00:50:15,793
I'm pretty good with fish too, right?

1235
00:50:16,563 --> 00:50:18,692
- This is more my calling. - Exactly.

1236
00:50:18,693 --> 00:50:20,533
(The two seriously consider changing careers.)

1237
00:50:21,763 --> 00:50:25,062
(But...)

1238
00:50:25,063 --> 00:50:27,203
(the gizzard shad aren't coming up?)

1239
00:50:27,873 --> 00:50:30,243
The gizzard shad aren't coming in large numbers.

1240
00:50:30,473 --> 00:50:32,442
- We're getting fewer now. - Something is coming up.

1241
00:50:32,443 --> 00:50:33,923
We're getting fewer gizzard shad now.

1242
00:50:34,913 --> 00:50:38,713
(The second net brings in a smaller catch.)

1243
00:50:39,243 --> 00:50:41,753
- Gizzard shad are hard to catch. - I see.

1244
00:50:42,453 --> 00:50:45,222
Gizzard shad are hard to catch these days.

1245
00:50:45,223 --> 00:50:46,822
- Are they? - Yes,

1246
00:50:46,823 --> 00:50:49,122
- they've become scarce this year. - Have they become scarce this year?

1247
00:50:49,123 --> 00:50:50,123
(Extreme heat means fewer fish.)

1248
00:50:50,124 --> 00:50:52,462
Oh, my. Catching gizzard shad isn't easy.

1249
00:50:52,463 --> 00:50:54,103
(Who knew gizzard shad were so precious?)

1250
00:50:54,593 --> 00:50:58,263
Gizzard shad, please come in droves!

1251
00:50:59,063 --> 00:51:02,372
(She desperately calls out for gizzard shad.)

1252
00:51:02,373 --> 00:51:04,273
Here they come.

1253
00:51:04,703 --> 00:51:07,872
(And right on cue, precious gizzard shad appear!)

1254
00:51:07,873 --> 00:51:10,943
Dear priceless gizzard shad, we'll treat you well.

1255
00:51:11,283 --> 00:51:13,242
Handle them gently,

1256
00:51:13,243 --> 00:51:15,413
so we don't snap their necks.

1257
00:51:16,413 --> 00:51:17,423
(Another valuable catch)

1258
00:51:19,823 --> 00:51:21,192
Dear priceless gizzard shad.

1259
00:51:21,193 --> 00:51:22,922
(Now that they know how precious gizzard shad are, )

1260
00:51:22,923 --> 00:51:27,863
(every single fish means even more.)

1261
00:51:27,963 --> 00:51:30,533
They are priceless. Be gentle with them.

1262
00:51:31,033 --> 00:51:34,173
Valuable gizzard shad, we will treat you gently.

1263
00:51:34,873 --> 00:51:38,042
- The sun is rising. - It's coming up. The sun is up now.

1264
00:51:38,043 --> 00:51:39,483
(The sun has already begun to rise.)

1265
00:51:39,603 --> 00:51:42,473
Really. Please come, gizzard shad.

1266
00:51:42,873 --> 00:51:45,812
Viewers, the sea is a mystery.

1267
00:51:45,813 --> 00:51:47,382
If only we could get five more.

1268
00:51:47,383 --> 00:51:49,252
(Out on the unpredictable sea, the nets are still empty.)

1269
00:51:49,253 --> 00:51:50,522
We're not getting many gizzard shad today.

1270
00:51:50,523 --> 00:51:52,483
- Here they come! - They're coming!

1271
00:51:54,193 --> 00:51:56,393
Okay.

1272
00:51:56,493 --> 00:51:57,762
Be careful not to hurt them.

1273
00:51:57,763 --> 00:51:59,022
- That's it. Good. - Done.

1274
00:51:59,023 --> 00:52:00,032
(Carefully removing each fish, 1 by 1)

1275
00:52:00,033 --> 00:52:01,933
- It's alive. - It's alive.

1276
00:52:02,493 --> 00:52:03,663
Come.

1277
00:52:03,933 --> 00:52:06,033
- Come here. - Here they are.

1278
00:52:06,603 --> 00:52:08,202
Let's fill up half the tank.

1279
00:52:08,203 --> 00:52:10,373
(Little by little, the pile of gizzard shad grows.)

1280
00:52:10,843 --> 00:52:12,542
Gently.

1281
00:52:12,543 --> 00:52:14,273
Don't harm any of them.

1282
00:52:15,143 --> 00:52:16,213
Here they are.

1283
00:52:16,313 --> 00:52:18,343
Here they are!

1284
00:52:18,643 --> 00:52:19,842
Gizzard shad.

1285
00:52:19,843 --> 00:52:21,852
- Two gizzard shad are coming up. - Here they come.

1286
00:52:21,853 --> 00:52:22,853
(They've been working since the early hours.)

1287
00:52:22,854 --> 00:52:25,482
- Here are the gizzard shad. - The gizzard shad are here.

1288
00:52:25,483 --> 00:52:26,623
- Here they are. - Nice.

1289
00:52:27,193 --> 00:52:29,423
- We're done with the nets. - We're done.

1290
00:52:29,493 --> 00:52:30,663
We're done.

1291
00:52:32,063 --> 00:52:33,732
Thank you.

1292
00:52:33,733 --> 00:52:36,033
- Are you exhausted? - No, I'm not.

1293
00:52:36,703 --> 00:52:38,663
We didn't get many gizzard shad.

1294
00:52:39,633 --> 00:52:40,732
I wanted to get more.

1295
00:52:40,733 --> 00:52:43,049
(Sun Young is disappointed they didn't get a bigger catch.)

1296
00:52:43,073 --> 00:52:45,173
(You Seok feels the same.)

1297
00:52:45,503 --> 00:52:48,072
It's a bummer that we didn't catch many.

1298
00:52:48,073 --> 00:52:49,919
(Experiencing the value of gizzard shad for themselves)

1299
00:52:49,943 --> 00:52:53,083
Can you cook the gizzard shad if we give you some?

1300
00:52:53,313 --> 00:52:55,953
- Are you giving some to us? - Yes, since you've worked hard.

1301
00:52:56,883 --> 00:52:59,222
- Thank you. - Thank you.

1302
00:52:59,223 --> 00:53:01,992
Can we really accept such valuable fish?

1303
00:53:01,993 --> 00:53:04,792
(The lady even prepares sashimi for the hardworking siblings.)

1304
00:53:04,793 --> 00:53:05,823
Amazing.

1305
00:53:06,063 --> 00:53:07,563
Visit us again next year!

1306
00:53:07,593 --> 00:53:09,563
Should we visit again next year?

1307
00:53:10,033 --> 00:53:11,062
We'll come to catch something else.

1308
00:53:11,063 --> 00:53:12,823
(May they fill the boat on their next trip!)

1309
00:53:13,033 --> 00:53:14,433
Try some with kimchi.

1310
00:53:15,703 --> 00:53:20,213
(Gizzard shad served with the lady's homemade kimchi)

1311
00:53:21,673 --> 00:53:22,812
Is it good?

1312
00:53:22,813 --> 00:53:24,773
(How does gizzard shad sashimi taste out at sea?)

1313
00:53:25,083 --> 00:53:26,143
It's hitting the spot.

1314
00:53:27,913 --> 00:53:28,913
You can taste the fat.

1315
00:53:28,914 --> 00:53:30,623
- Is it good? - It's good.

1316
00:53:32,153 --> 00:53:35,123
(Settling in for a full-on eating show)

1317
00:53:36,053 --> 00:53:38,263
(Hooked on gizzard shad)

1318
00:53:38,793 --> 00:53:40,762
(Everyone needs to try this!)

1319
00:53:40,763 --> 00:53:42,563
Do you want another one? Do you want it?

1320
00:53:43,733 --> 00:53:44,733
It's really good.

1321
00:53:44,734 --> 00:53:47,532
Ma'am, the kimchi is amazing.

1322
00:53:47,533 --> 00:53:48,673
Is it?

1323
00:53:49,273 --> 00:53:50,343
Really?

1324
00:53:50,843 --> 00:53:53,042
My gosh, and these gizzard shad are rare.

1325
00:53:53,043 --> 00:53:54,872
- Take it. - Thank you.

1326
00:53:54,873 --> 00:53:57,042
- Come again next year. - Thank you. Okay.

1327
00:53:57,043 --> 00:53:59,482
(The lady even gave them a box of freshly caught gizzard shad.)

1328
00:53:59,483 --> 00:54:02,853
Thank you. Bye.

1329
00:54:03,623 --> 00:54:04,982
- Thank you. - Bye. See you next year.

1330
00:54:04,983 --> 00:54:06,322
- Okay. Thank you for the fish. - Take care.

1331
00:54:06,323 --> 00:54:08,353
- Thank you. - Bye.

1332
00:54:09,423 --> 00:54:12,893
(Utterly drained)

1333
00:54:12,993 --> 00:54:14,962
You guys had to come out at dawn...

1334
00:54:14,963 --> 00:54:16,663
to catch gizzard shad. So good work.

1335
00:54:16,933 --> 00:54:18,262
(It's time to get paid for their labor.)

1336
00:54:18,263 --> 00:54:19,903
- Let's check how much we earned. - Yes.

1337
00:54:20,673 --> 00:54:23,603
One, two, three, four, five...

1338
00:54:24,203 --> 00:54:25,442
- Ten. - One hundred dollars.

1339
00:54:25,443 --> 00:54:26,473
One hundred dollars.

1340
00:54:26,773 --> 00:54:28,133
- Yesterday... - You paid us well.

1341
00:54:29,013 --> 00:54:31,183
It was really fun, though. I mean it.

1342
00:54:31,743 --> 00:54:33,659
When would we get a chance to get on a boat late at night?

1343
00:54:33,683 --> 00:54:35,082
Right. It was really fun.

1344
00:54:35,083 --> 00:54:36,523
Gizzard shad is a hard one to catch.

1345
00:54:37,023 --> 00:54:38,123
No way. My gosh.

1346
00:54:38,923 --> 00:54:41,592
It's such a difficult one to catch.

1347
00:54:41,593 --> 00:54:43,892
Gizzard shad is hard to catch, but very delicious.

1348
00:54:43,893 --> 00:54:46,192
(Fresh and lively gizzard shad, )

1349
00:54:46,193 --> 00:54:48,463
(bursting with rich ocean flavor...)

1350
00:54:50,063 --> 00:54:53,632
(was shipped across the country.)

1351
00:54:53,633 --> 00:54:56,803
My goodness. Look at that. The sun is rising brightly.

1352
00:54:57,003 --> 00:54:58,683
- Right. - Gosh, what a rewarding morning.

1353
00:54:59,043 --> 00:55:00,813
Right? We left at dawn.

1354
00:55:01,043 --> 00:55:03,142
- Exactly. - We left at dawn.

1355
00:55:03,143 --> 00:55:05,263
(A rewarding day of early morning work and a sunrise)

1356
00:55:06,413 --> 00:55:08,413
My goodness. The gazebo here is so beautiful.

1357
00:55:08,783 --> 00:55:10,553
Gosh, what a beautiful gazebo.

1358
00:55:10,823 --> 00:55:13,023
Goodness, we're going to wrap them in a beautiful spot.

1359
00:55:13,723 --> 00:55:15,753
Are they beans or bean sprouts?

1360
00:55:15,923 --> 00:55:17,723
- They're peas. - You're right.

1361
00:55:18,063 --> 00:55:20,563
- They're peas. - They're peas? Really?

1362
00:55:21,463 --> 00:55:22,862
- What is it? - It's a wisteria tree.

1363
00:55:22,863 --> 00:55:24,732
- It's just fruit. - Fruit.

1364
00:55:24,733 --> 00:55:26,662
- This... - White flowers bloom from the tree.

1365
00:55:26,663 --> 00:55:29,033
Then the tree bears fruit later.

1366
00:55:29,833 --> 00:55:31,472
- They look like peas. - Yes.

1367
00:55:31,473 --> 00:55:33,443
(The flowers look beautiful.)

1368
00:55:33,673 --> 00:55:36,372
Should we put down the ones we harvested here?

1369
00:55:36,373 --> 00:55:38,442
- Or... - Put them here. And...

1370
00:55:38,443 --> 00:55:40,383
Let me put on the gloves. It's not good.

1371
00:55:41,283 --> 00:55:43,282
Put them in the box nicely like this.

1372
00:55:43,283 --> 00:55:44,382
- Right here. - Nicely.

1373
00:55:44,383 --> 00:55:45,383
Like this.

1374
00:55:45,523 --> 00:55:49,253
(Neatly pack the figs in the box with the bottom side facing up.)

1375
00:55:49,523 --> 00:55:51,793
- Put small ones on the bottom. - I know how to do this.

1376
00:55:52,193 --> 00:55:54,393
Then put big ones on top.

1377
00:55:55,233 --> 00:55:57,502
So they hold the structure like this.

1378
00:55:57,503 --> 00:55:59,232
That way, they're not going to topple over.

1379
00:55:59,233 --> 00:56:00,973
So they keep their structure.

1380
00:56:01,503 --> 00:56:03,973
So make two layers. Put big ones on top.

1381
00:56:04,173 --> 00:56:06,172
I see. That way, the structure stays supported.

1382
00:56:06,173 --> 00:56:07,342
The structure is supported then.

1383
00:56:07,343 --> 00:56:10,183
(It's over once they securely stack them up in an alternating pattern.)

1384
00:56:10,983 --> 00:56:12,043
- Like this. - Okay.

1385
00:56:12,613 --> 00:56:14,953
- I know how to do this. - Put small ones on the bottom.

1386
00:56:15,283 --> 00:56:16,812
So we don't have to put a specific number of figs in it?

1387
00:56:16,813 --> 00:56:18,222
We just have to fill it up?

1388
00:56:18,223 --> 00:56:19,582
- We just have to fill it up, right? - Right.

1389
00:56:19,583 --> 00:56:21,653
Fill up the box and wrap it nicely like this.

1390
00:56:22,053 --> 00:56:23,792
So that's 1kg?

1391
00:56:23,793 --> 00:56:25,693
(A full box should weigh 1kg.)

1392
00:56:26,093 --> 00:56:27,762
- Give it a try. - Let's try it. Okay. I got it.

1393
00:56:27,763 --> 00:56:29,493
- So... - We'll be neat.

1394
00:56:29,763 --> 00:56:31,323
- Put in small ones first. - Then we...

1395
00:56:31,933 --> 00:56:33,532
The 3 of us should do 1 together.

1396
00:56:33,533 --> 00:56:35,903
- Let's fill the box together. - Where...

1397
00:56:36,003 --> 00:56:37,602
- Someone has to hold that. - Yes.

1398
00:56:37,603 --> 00:56:39,002
- Yes. You're right. - Yes. That should be faster.

1399
00:56:39,003 --> 00:56:40,243
- That should be faster. - Yes.

1400
00:56:41,043 --> 00:56:43,643
(Figs can easily slide around when you pack them alone.)

1401
00:56:43,783 --> 00:56:45,442
You're so smart.

1402
00:56:45,443 --> 00:56:46,712
(Suggesting a division of labor after understanding the task)

1403
00:56:46,713 --> 00:56:48,153
The three of us will work as a team.

1404
00:56:49,083 --> 00:56:50,083
Here.

1405
00:56:50,083 --> 00:56:51,083
(Passing over)

1406
00:56:51,423 --> 00:56:55,993
(He's in charge of selecting and passing over the figs.)

1407
00:56:57,163 --> 00:56:58,193
Thank you.

1408
00:56:59,623 --> 00:57:00,892
(The art major, Yoon Seo, )

1409
00:57:00,893 --> 00:57:04,463
(is in charge of placing them inside the box.)

1410
00:57:04,763 --> 00:57:06,283
- I'll hold it. - You have to hold it.

1411
00:57:06,863 --> 00:57:09,203
(Holding the figs bottom-side up)

1412
00:57:09,773 --> 00:57:13,073
(Jung Ah is in charge of assisting the fig placement.)

1413
00:57:13,503 --> 00:57:14,613
Let's pick up the speed.

1414
00:57:15,913 --> 00:57:17,013
We'll finish pretty fast.

1415
00:57:18,713 --> 00:57:20,653
Here you go. It's done. Right?

1416
00:57:22,053 --> 00:57:23,782
We have to pay you guys for the work afterwards.

1417
00:57:23,783 --> 00:57:24,853
- Yes. - Right.

1418
00:57:25,253 --> 00:57:27,923
We'll pay you two dollars...

1419
00:57:28,393 --> 00:57:29,622
for each box you pack.

1420
00:57:29,623 --> 00:57:30,923
Two dollars per box?

1421
00:57:31,963 --> 00:57:34,092
Don't you think this division of labor is working out well?

1422
00:57:34,093 --> 00:57:35,093
You bet.

1423
00:57:35,733 --> 00:57:37,063
That goes without saying.

1424
00:57:37,363 --> 00:57:38,663
That goes without saying?

1425
00:57:39,663 --> 00:57:43,172
(Smooth)

1426
00:57:43,173 --> 00:57:44,272
This is good.

1427
00:57:44,273 --> 00:57:47,413
(Boxes of figs are quickly stacking up.)

1428
00:57:49,073 --> 00:57:50,543
The way You Seok flirts is so funny.

1429
00:57:51,183 --> 00:57:52,342
- He's got no game. - Exactly.

1430
00:57:52,343 --> 00:57:53,482
It's like he's never done it before.

1431
00:57:53,483 --> 00:57:54,483
- Right? - Yes.

1432
00:57:54,484 --> 00:57:55,852
I kind of get the feeling he's never had a girlfriend.

1433
00:57:55,853 --> 00:57:58,583
(I kind of get the feeling he's never had a girlfriend.)

1434
00:57:58,823 --> 00:58:00,822
When he hears that, he's going to pout.

1435
00:58:00,823 --> 00:58:02,393
(Pouting hard)

1436
00:58:02,623 --> 00:58:03,653
"That's not true."

1437
00:58:03,763 --> 00:58:05,243
"You think I never had a girlfriend?"

1438
00:58:05,663 --> 00:58:06,693
"Jung Ah!"

1439
00:58:07,863 --> 00:58:09,893
"Should I call up my ex-girlfriends?"

1440
00:58:10,933 --> 00:58:13,163
"Yes, do it."

1441
00:58:13,633 --> 00:58:15,403
Your impression was spot on.

1442
00:58:16,303 --> 00:58:17,942
I thought he was here for a second.

1443
00:58:17,943 --> 00:58:19,003
(Goofing around)

1444
00:58:20,103 --> 00:58:23,843
(Their hands keep on moving while enjoying their conversation.)

1445
00:58:24,643 --> 00:58:27,013
Gosh. At this rate, we'll earn 200 dollars again.

1446
00:58:27,653 --> 00:58:29,413
- Oh, my. - What will they do?

1447
00:58:30,013 --> 00:58:33,223
(A huge pile of fig boxes)

1448
00:58:33,553 --> 00:58:35,253
You guys will need a lot of cash again.

1449
00:58:35,753 --> 00:58:37,363
Oh, my. I bet you guys are surprised.

1450
00:58:38,223 --> 00:58:40,633
We always exceed your expectations.

1451
00:58:42,033 --> 00:58:43,693
We're picking up the speed now.

1452
00:58:46,663 --> 00:58:49,333
(The huge box that was full of figs is now empty.)

1453
00:58:49,673 --> 00:58:50,673
(Oh, my)

1454
00:58:50,803 --> 00:58:52,449
- They might topple over. - They might topple over.

1455
00:58:52,473 --> 00:58:54,273
- Put that down there. - I can't stack it up.

1456
00:58:54,873 --> 00:58:55,943
No way.

1457
00:58:56,313 --> 00:58:57,882
We're done now.

1458
00:58:57,883 --> 00:58:59,189
(The other baskets are empty too.)

1459
00:58:59,213 --> 00:59:00,313
We harvested a lot of figs.

1460
00:59:01,613 --> 00:59:03,512
One, two, three, four, five,

1461
00:59:03,513 --> 00:59:05,653
six, seven, eight, nine, and ten.

1462
00:59:05,723 --> 00:59:07,563
- We packed a lot of boxes. - That's 40 boxes.

1463
00:59:07,623 --> 00:59:08,753
Here's ten more.

1464
00:59:09,293 --> 00:59:10,352
- Fifty boxes. - What's the total?

1465
00:59:10,353 --> 00:59:12,339
- Fifty boxes. One hundred dollars. - Fifty boxes.

1466
00:59:12,363 --> 00:59:13,692
We earned 100 dollars.

1467
00:59:13,693 --> 00:59:15,433
Gosh. And we were fast too.

1468
00:59:15,793 --> 00:59:17,902
- Here you go. - Thank you.

1469
00:59:17,903 --> 00:59:18,933
Thank you.

1470
00:59:20,163 --> 00:59:21,302
Did you finish?

1471
00:59:21,303 --> 00:59:23,073
- Thank you. Yes. We finished. - Yes.

1472
00:59:23,273 --> 00:59:24,553
Take this home and have a taste.

1473
00:59:24,643 --> 00:59:26,202
- My gosh. You already gave us some. - Thank you.

1474
00:59:26,203 --> 00:59:27,843
- This too. - Thank you.

1475
00:59:28,073 --> 00:59:29,272
- Thank you for the figs. - Thank you for the figs.

1476
00:59:29,273 --> 00:59:30,793
- Thank you. - Thank you for the figs.

1477
00:59:30,983 --> 00:59:32,683
Gosh, she gave us a present too.

1478
00:59:32,983 --> 00:59:34,343
- They're going to love it. - Yes.

1479
00:59:35,513 --> 00:59:37,583
Let's show them these delicious figs.

1480
00:59:37,653 --> 00:59:38,852
- Let's go. - Let's go.

1481
00:59:38,853 --> 00:59:39,853
- Let's go. - Let's hurry.

1482
00:59:39,854 --> 00:59:41,893
Seriously. This is a complicated feeling.

1483
00:59:42,423 --> 00:59:44,392
I can't believe it's morning now.

1484
00:59:44,393 --> 00:59:46,622
Is it 9am? It's not 9am yet, right?

1485
00:59:46,623 --> 00:59:47,633
No.

1486
00:59:49,333 --> 00:59:53,063
(The aromatic and fresh figs were shipped to the consumers.)

1487
00:59:53,433 --> 00:59:54,732
Let's put them in the fridge.

1488
00:59:54,733 --> 00:59:56,603
- So they can have it cold. - Yes.

1489
00:59:56,933 --> 00:59:58,902
But we have so much food in the fridge.

1490
00:59:58,903 --> 00:59:59,903
Right.

1491
01:00:00,303 --> 01:00:03,443
We have so much food. I wonder if we can finish everything.

1492
01:00:03,613 --> 01:00:08,153
(After the fig harvest which made them feel rich and generous...)

1493
01:00:08,813 --> 01:00:09,913
Get some sleep.

1494
01:00:12,653 --> 01:00:18,163
(Team Gizzard Shad has returned and is sleeping.)

1495
01:00:18,463 --> 01:00:20,833
(Team Fig arrives shortly.)

1496
01:00:21,063 --> 01:00:22,863
- I guess they're sleeping. - Okay.

1497
01:00:24,363 --> 01:00:25,562
No one is here.

1498
01:00:25,563 --> 01:00:26,833
(Loud)

1499
01:00:27,433 --> 01:00:30,002
No. They're sleeping. They left early in the morning.

1500
01:00:30,003 --> 01:00:31,902
- They're just resting. - It's breezy.

1501
01:00:31,903 --> 01:00:34,103
(They quietly go in the house after figuring that out.)

1502
01:00:34,373 --> 01:00:36,143
(Careful)

1503
01:00:38,843 --> 01:00:42,953
(Team Fig also tries to get some sleep quietly.)

1504
01:00:43,583 --> 01:00:46,753
(After a two-hour break, )

1505
01:00:47,153 --> 01:00:50,153
(the younger ones are still catching up on sleep...)

1506
01:00:51,093 --> 01:00:53,463
(and Jung Ah wakes up.)

1507
01:00:54,263 --> 01:00:57,203
(She stretches her back.)

1508
01:00:57,763 --> 01:01:01,403
(She puts on a headband to look neat.)

1509
01:01:01,833 --> 01:01:05,703
(She carefully leaves the room not to wake the others up.)

1510
01:01:06,173 --> 01:01:09,572
(She makes a cup of coffee since she's up.)

1511
01:01:09,573 --> 01:01:11,283
- Jung Ah. - You startled me.

1512
01:01:11,583 --> 01:01:12,913
You startled me!

1513
01:01:13,843 --> 01:01:16,183
(Yes, it worked.)

1514
01:01:17,013 --> 01:01:19,782
(Not to wake up the others, )

1515
01:01:19,783 --> 01:01:22,493
(the two of them step outside.)

1516
01:01:22,793 --> 01:01:26,393
(They enjoy their coffee on the veranda.)

1517
01:01:26,723 --> 01:01:28,893
- Isn't this place amazing? - I'm happy.

1518
01:01:31,633 --> 01:01:34,673
(As they enjoy the view that brings them joy, )

1519
01:01:36,333 --> 01:01:40,443
(lunchtime is approaching fast.)

1520
01:01:40,943 --> 01:01:43,713
(Yoon Seo is already up.)

1521
01:01:44,013 --> 01:01:46,912
(Sun Young is still fast asleep.)

1522
01:01:46,913 --> 01:01:48,313
The princess is still sleeping?

1523
01:01:48,483 --> 01:01:49,613
Wait. Is she up?

1524
01:01:50,253 --> 01:01:52,722
- Princess? - Let me this princess sleep more.

1525
01:01:52,723 --> 01:01:54,223
Princess. My gosh.

1526
01:01:54,993 --> 01:01:56,553
- Show me your T-shirt. - Here.

1527
01:01:57,423 --> 01:01:59,893
(My T-shirt?)

1528
01:02:00,363 --> 01:02:01,863
That's so cute.

1529
01:02:02,193 --> 01:02:03,432
I mean...

1530
01:02:03,433 --> 01:02:05,663
(Her inner thought is printed on the T-shirt.)

1531
01:02:06,163 --> 01:02:07,163
That's cute.

1532
01:02:07,164 --> 01:02:09,033
- The T-shirt... - I didn't...

1533
01:02:09,233 --> 01:02:10,303
That's cute.

1534
01:02:11,203 --> 01:02:12,443
What did you guys do?

1535
01:02:12,773 --> 01:02:13,872
We harvested figs.

1536
01:02:13,873 --> 01:02:15,042
- Did you bring some back? - Yes.

1537
01:02:15,043 --> 01:02:16,589
- I love figs? - They're in the fridge.

1538
01:02:16,613 --> 01:02:17,712
But we brought a lot.

1539
01:02:17,713 --> 01:02:18,843
(Kim Sun Young: Fig Fanatic)

1540
01:02:19,183 --> 01:02:21,252
- It was so good. - I love figs.

1541
01:02:21,253 --> 01:02:22,753
- Do you want some now? - Yes.

1542
01:02:23,213 --> 01:02:24,582
- Let me bring you some. - We have a lot of figs.

1543
01:02:24,583 --> 01:02:26,052
Let's just gently rinse them...

1544
01:02:26,053 --> 01:02:27,223
- and eat. - Sure.

1545
01:02:27,393 --> 01:02:29,222
