01:22:38,747 --> 01:22:40,677
(the art major is very careful unlike Sang Hun.)

2053
01:22:41,377 --> 01:22:42,416
(Her posture screams art major.)

2054
01:22:42,417 --> 01:22:43,647
I'll go this way.

2055
01:22:45,087 --> 01:22:46,316
An orca.

2056
01:22:46,317 --> 01:22:48,477
(After the simulation, she draws a sketch of an orca.)

2057
01:22:48,927 --> 01:22:50,556
(Delicate)

2058
01:22:50,557 --> 01:22:51,687
After that...

2059
01:22:52,527 --> 01:22:55,697
(Do you think you'll find students like her if you major in art?)

2060
01:22:56,167 --> 01:22:57,396
(No!)

2061
01:22:57,397 --> 01:23:01,197
(Yoon Seo is the only one.)

2062
01:23:02,307 --> 01:23:05,406
(After drawing like an art major, )

2063
01:23:05,407 --> 01:23:08,137
Its eye is over here.

2064
01:23:09,007 --> 01:23:10,946
(the orca sketch is ready.)

2065
01:23:10,947 --> 01:23:12,117
That's done.

2066
01:23:12,517 --> 01:23:13,647
What's next?

2067
01:23:14,817 --> 01:23:16,417
Clams and starfish.

2068
01:23:17,487 --> 01:23:19,417
I need to sketch the boat too.

2069
01:23:20,257 --> 01:23:22,157
- It'll take a lot of time. - Right?

2070
01:23:22,257 --> 01:23:23,257
Yes.

2071
01:23:23,557 --> 01:23:26,297
(Let's speed up.)

2072
01:23:26,457 --> 01:23:28,197
I'll draw cute ones.

2073
01:23:28,897 --> 01:23:29,927
Patrick Star.

2074
01:23:30,167 --> 01:23:32,567
(From cute starfish...)

2075
01:23:32,967 --> 01:23:36,337
Clams. It's been a while since I drew with this much effort.

2076
01:23:39,777 --> 01:23:41,807
(The siblings' Bob Ross...)

2077
01:23:42,347 --> 01:23:43,606
(added a big fish.)

2078
01:23:43,607 --> 01:23:45,177
Gosh, Sang Hun. It's so cute.

2079
01:23:45,677 --> 01:23:48,116
He's crazy.

2080
01:23:48,117 --> 01:23:49,317
He's so good.

2081
01:23:49,717 --> 01:23:50,846
Don't say that.

2082
01:23:50,847 --> 01:23:53,256
I'm just drawing what I saw.

2083
01:23:53,257 --> 01:23:54,777
(A genius with hidden drawing talents)

2084
01:23:54,857 --> 01:23:57,957
(As Bob Ross and the art major joined forces, )

2085
01:23:58,797 --> 01:23:59,996
Did we fill it up too much?

2086
01:23:59,997 --> 01:24:01,633
(the sketching process is going smoothly.)

2087
01:24:01,657 --> 01:24:03,996
(Meanwhile, in the kitchen...)

2088
01:24:03,997 --> 01:24:06,166
What are we doing right now?

2089
01:24:06,167 --> 01:24:09,107
We'll prep the vegetables we will use today.

2090
01:24:09,467 --> 01:24:11,006
We'll gather them in one place...

2091
01:24:11,007 --> 01:24:12,567
so that we can grab what we need later.

2092
01:24:13,377 --> 01:24:14,576
(Jung Ah grabs the green onions.)

2093
01:24:14,577 --> 01:24:15,977
We'll use them later.

2094
01:24:17,177 --> 01:24:19,917
(You Seok grabs the onions.)

2095
01:24:20,417 --> 01:24:23,747
(Each of them takes a vegetable to prep.)

2096
01:24:24,317 --> 01:24:26,117
(She rinses the green onions thoroughly.)

2097
01:24:26,457 --> 01:24:27,956
(She cuts them to a manageable size...)

2098
01:24:27,957 --> 01:24:32,027
(and stakes them up.)

2099
01:24:32,327 --> 01:24:34,497
No one's using the potatoes. Right, You Seok?

2100
01:24:35,057 --> 01:24:36,266
I don't think so.

2101
01:24:36,267 --> 01:24:37,896
I should wash some chilis, right?

2102
01:24:37,897 --> 01:24:39,796
We'll use many chilis. I'm going to use them too.

2103
01:24:39,797 --> 01:24:40,967
We'll need chilis.

2104
01:24:41,567 --> 01:24:43,306
(She preps each ingredient calmly...)

2105
01:24:43,307 --> 01:24:45,167
(after checking what each participant needs.)

2106
01:24:45,807 --> 01:24:48,036
(Meanwhile, You Seok is in the yard, prepping the onions.)

2107
01:24:48,037 --> 01:24:49,707
What I'm making today is...

2108
01:24:50,347 --> 01:24:51,477
suyuk.

2109
01:24:52,347 --> 01:24:54,447
We'll use pork for the cooking match today.

2110
01:24:55,047 --> 01:24:56,647
- Come to think of it, - Dear viewers...

2111
01:24:56,847 --> 01:24:58,717
making bossam won't be enough.

2112
01:24:59,457 --> 01:25:01,057
I'm going to add some other ingredients.

2113
01:25:01,257 --> 01:25:05,227
I'll show you in detail later on.

2114
01:25:05,427 --> 01:25:06,697
Who are you talking to?

2115
01:25:06,857 --> 01:25:08,197
Our viewers.

2116
01:25:08,497 --> 01:25:09,897
(She's used to it.)

2117
01:25:10,097 --> 01:25:11,296
I'm used to it now.

2118
01:25:11,297 --> 01:25:12,673
(It's not new to see the siblings resembling one another.)

2119
01:25:12,697 --> 01:25:14,296
This is what I'm going to do.

2120
01:25:14,297 --> 01:25:15,443
(The cooking briefing isn't over yet.)

2121
01:25:15,467 --> 01:25:17,837
I'm going to sear both sides of the meat slightly...

2122
01:25:18,777 --> 01:25:20,837
until the Maillard reaction kicks in.

2123
01:25:21,807 --> 01:25:24,377
I'll sear it before I boil it.

2124
01:25:25,717 --> 01:25:28,417
It'll be crispy on the outside and juicy on the inside.

2125
01:25:29,017 --> 01:25:31,116
Two, four, six. Eight onions will be enough, right?

2126
01:25:31,117 --> 01:25:33,093
(He aims to take 1st place with his home cooking experience.)

2127
01:25:33,117 --> 01:25:34,887
- Will you cook the rice? - Yes.

2128
01:25:38,287 --> 01:25:40,297
- Will white rice work best? - Yes.

2129
01:25:40,727 --> 01:25:42,887
We should make white rice that goes with their dishes.

2130
01:25:43,267 --> 01:25:45,297
This is what worries me. As for suyuk,

2131
01:25:45,997 --> 01:25:47,796
the longer you boil it, the tastier it gets.

2132
01:25:47,797 --> 01:25:49,683
(The original king of communication comes to rinse rice.)

2133
01:25:49,707 --> 01:25:50,766
You're here.

2134
01:25:50,767 --> 01:25:52,737
- Yes, hello. Are you here to shoot? - Yes.

2135
01:25:53,037 --> 01:25:54,306
(Acting politely to the master of skits)

2136
01:25:54,307 --> 01:25:55,977
I was talking to the viewers.

2137
01:25:56,477 --> 01:25:58,007
- You're an actor, aren't you? - Me?

2138
01:25:58,077 --> 01:26:00,247
Yes. I think I saw you on TV.

2139
01:26:01,217 --> 01:26:03,487
I'm not an actor. I'm a fisherman.

2140
01:26:03,587 --> 01:26:04,747
- Are you a fisherman? - Yes.

2141
01:26:05,117 --> 01:26:06,157
Me too.

2142
01:26:06,357 --> 01:26:07,886
I fish gizzard shad for a living.

2143
01:26:07,887 --> 01:26:08,956
- Really? - Yes.

2144
01:26:08,957 --> 01:26:10,486
- So do I. - Really?

2145
01:26:10,487 --> 01:26:12,957
I'm a captain of a boat right here.

2146
01:26:13,127 --> 01:26:16,096
- I see. Let's work together soon. - Let's get going!

2147
01:26:16,097 --> 01:26:17,697
Come and ride my boat sometime.

2148
01:26:18,227 --> 01:26:19,967
Who will use the napa cabbage?

2149
01:26:20,837 --> 01:26:22,667
Who's using the napa cabbage? Sang Hun?

2150
01:26:22,837 --> 01:26:25,036
Yes. You can just wash them.

2151
01:26:25,037 --> 01:26:26,477
- I'll wash them. - Don't chop them.

2152
01:26:28,237 --> 01:26:29,306
The peeler.

2153
01:26:29,307 --> 01:26:31,677
(She preps the carrots next.)

2154
01:26:32,377 --> 01:26:34,247
(Thinking carefully)

2155
01:26:34,977 --> 01:26:36,747
Jung Ah, the bean sprouts.

2156
01:26:37,147 --> 01:26:38,416
We don't put carrots...

2157
01:26:38,417 --> 01:26:40,137
in the spicy pork with bean sprouts, do we?

2158
01:26:40,187 --> 01:26:41,516
Didn't you read the recipe?

2159
01:26:41,517 --> 01:26:43,457
(What are you talking about?)

2160
01:26:43,857 --> 01:26:47,027
It's up to you whether to put them in.

2161
01:26:47,857 --> 01:26:49,497
I need to follow my own recipe.

2162
01:26:49,727 --> 01:26:51,497
What do you think?

2163
01:26:52,897 --> 01:26:54,196
You shouldn't put them in.

2164
01:26:54,197 --> 01:26:55,477
(Answering her without thinking)

2165
01:26:55,937 --> 01:26:56,966
Exactly.

2166
01:26:56,967 --> 01:26:58,713
(She smoothly identified the judge's preference.)

2167
01:26:58,737 --> 01:27:00,876
(Nonchalant)

2168
01:27:00,877 --> 01:27:02,246
(She plans to win again...)

2169
01:27:02,247 --> 01:27:04,447
(after letting everyone's guard down.)

2170
01:27:05,677 --> 01:27:08,577
(1st place is mine.)

2171
01:27:09,117 --> 01:27:11,587
(Fired up to win, they finish prepping the ingredients.)

2172
01:27:12,387 --> 01:27:14,087
We're done with prepping, right?

2173
01:27:14,387 --> 01:27:15,417
Yes.

2174
01:27:15,627 --> 01:27:17,086
We should check...

2175
01:27:17,087 --> 01:27:19,496
how they're doing and help them.

2176
01:27:19,497 --> 01:27:20,927
I'll go and see.

2177
01:27:21,527 --> 01:27:22,966
(While the older sisters are wrapping up, )

2178
01:27:22,967 --> 01:27:24,397
(You Seok leaves the house first.)

2179
01:27:25,267 --> 01:27:26,296
Good.

2180
01:27:26,297 --> 01:27:27,643
(Sang Hun and Yoon Seo are checking the progress.)

2181
01:27:27,667 --> 01:27:29,106
Will you draw another fish...

2182
01:27:29,107 --> 01:27:30,107
- over there? - Okay.

2183
01:27:30,108 --> 01:27:31,267
- At the end. - Okay.

2184
01:27:31,407 --> 01:27:33,807
(Carrying out the order)

2185
01:27:34,137 --> 01:27:35,437
I'm going to draw the boat.

2186
01:27:36,947 --> 01:27:39,517
(They're almost done with the sketches.)

2187
01:27:39,817 --> 01:27:41,276
Who said it was okay to paint a mural?

2188
01:27:41,277 --> 01:27:43,417
(Who said it was okay to paint a mural?)

2189
01:27:43,847 --> 01:27:45,716
(An intruder disrupts the peaceful mural painting.)

2190
01:27:45,717 --> 01:27:47,187
Goodness. Who are you?

2191
01:27:47,387 --> 01:27:50,186
The village chief gave us permission to paint here.

2192
01:27:50,187 --> 01:27:51,287
I'm the village chief.

2193
01:27:52,727 --> 01:27:54,627
Are you? You're young.

2194
01:27:55,627 --> 01:27:58,027
Where did you get that T-shirt?

2195
01:27:58,497 --> 01:27:59,867
It's been upgraded quite a bit.

2196
01:28:01,437 --> 01:28:02,606
(The goal of the young village chief is...)

2197
01:28:02,607 --> 01:28:03,607
Awesome.

2198
01:28:03,707 --> 01:28:05,137
I'm here to draw a turtle.

2199
01:28:05,537 --> 01:28:06,877
Right. The turtle.

2200
01:28:07,007 --> 01:28:08,907
You can draw it somewhere over here.

2201
01:28:09,577 --> 01:28:11,647
- It's a bit hard. - Yes.

2202
01:28:12,007 --> 01:28:14,347
- Will I be able to draw it? - Do you want me to do it?

2203
01:28:14,477 --> 01:28:16,717
Please modify it if I fail.

2204
01:28:17,087 --> 01:28:18,286
- Okay. - I'll try it first.

2205
01:28:18,287 --> 01:28:19,557
(He's a bit nervous, )

2206
01:28:19,987 --> 01:28:22,187
(but he goes for it, trusting Teacher Yoon Seo.)

2207
01:28:22,627 --> 01:28:25,757
(Despite the concerns, his hands keep moving.)

2208
01:28:26,127 --> 01:28:27,196
(Puckering)

2209
01:28:27,197 --> 01:28:29,427
(Concentrating hard with pursed lips)

2210
01:28:30,727 --> 01:28:32,697
- What do you think, Yoon Seo? - What?

2211
01:28:33,597 --> 01:28:34,997
Gosh. How come you're so good?

2212
01:28:35,237 --> 01:28:37,066
- Is it all right? - Why are you so good?

2213
01:28:37,067 --> 01:28:39,037
Did everyone study art?

2214
01:28:39,937 --> 01:28:41,076
(Beaming at the teacher's praise)

2215
01:28:41,077 --> 01:28:43,306
- What's with everyone? - Is it too small, though?

2216
01:28:43,307 --> 01:28:44,347
No.

2217
01:28:44,807 --> 01:28:45,876
Is it all right?

2218
01:28:45,877 --> 01:28:47,797
(I don't know who drew it, but it's quite nice.)

2219
01:28:47,847 --> 01:28:50,117
- Should I add some seagulls? - Yes. Good idea.

2220
01:28:51,147 --> 01:28:54,217
(Compliments allow You Seok to keep drawing.)

2221
01:28:54,587 --> 01:28:57,027
(Teacher Yoon Seo focuses again.)

2222
01:28:57,487 --> 01:28:59,657
(They've been drawing for 1 hour.)

2223
01:28:59,897 --> 01:29:00,927
Gosh, it's hot.

2224
01:29:01,697 --> 01:29:04,467
Gosh. This sunlight.

2225
01:29:04,797 --> 01:29:07,167
(Sweat is pouring down.)

2226
01:29:07,637 --> 01:29:08,696
Gosh. I'm sweating.

2227
01:29:08,697 --> 01:29:10,037
(But she can't stop drawing.)

2228
01:29:10,537 --> 01:29:12,707
(They draw hard without a break.)

2229
01:29:13,207 --> 01:29:14,236
Should I color it?

2230
01:29:14,237 --> 01:29:16,077
Yes. I think you can start coloring it.

2231
01:29:16,947 --> 01:29:19,247
Which color is easy to use?

2232
01:29:19,947 --> 01:29:22,517
(Which color will suit the mural?)

2233
01:29:24,187 --> 01:29:27,287
(He tests out the color yellow after thinking for a while.)

2234
01:29:30,587 --> 01:29:33,497
I'll start with this one. The yellow pops out.

2235
01:29:33,897 --> 01:29:36,097
(Serious)

2236
01:29:36,227 --> 01:29:37,396
I'm going to color it.

2237
01:29:37,397 --> 01:29:39,197
(He starts coloring it without hesitation.)

2238
01:29:40,037 --> 01:29:42,606
(On the blue waves, )

2239
01:29:42,607 --> 01:29:45,037
(a splash of bright yellow is added.)

2240
01:29:45,907 --> 01:29:50,677
(He's painting it with the color he chose.)

2241
01:29:51,347 --> 01:29:53,447
- It's so pretty, Sang Hun. - What?

2242
01:29:54,117 --> 01:29:55,676
I was drawing really slowly.

2243
01:29:55,677 --> 01:29:58,017
(Yoon Seo finishes sketching the boat in a hurry.)

2244
01:29:58,647 --> 01:30:00,457
Which color should I paint the boat with?

2245
01:30:01,487 --> 01:30:03,807
- Usually, the boats are white. - Should I paint it white?

2246
01:30:03,957 --> 01:30:06,057
I'll use white. I'll paint it white for now.

2247
01:30:06,457 --> 01:30:07,756
Are you going to color it right now?

2248
01:30:07,757 --> 01:30:09,027
I'm done with the sketches.

2249
01:30:10,097 --> 01:30:12,537
(What's going on in the house?)

2250
01:30:13,397 --> 01:30:14,467
This is fun.

2251
01:30:15,497 --> 01:30:17,136
(Sun Young, in excitement, )

2252
01:30:17,137 --> 01:30:19,207
(is flooding the yard with water.)

2253
01:30:19,637 --> 01:30:21,283
In the countryside, they splash water in the yard...

2254
01:30:21,307 --> 01:30:22,377
when it's hot.

2255
01:30:23,407 --> 01:30:25,076
I did that when I was young...

2256
01:30:25,077 --> 01:30:26,316
(She's cooling the yard off because it's hot.)

2257
01:30:26,317 --> 01:30:27,516
to lower the temperature.

2258
01:30:27,517 --> 01:30:29,357
(She's cooling the yard off because it's hot.)

2259
01:30:30,217 --> 01:30:31,247
Yes. That's right.

2260
01:30:33,887 --> 01:30:35,256
It looks cooler after that.

2261
01:30:35,257 --> 01:30:37,297
(The refreshing splash cools you just by watching.)

2262
01:30:37,657 --> 01:30:39,097
Who wants to get splashed?

2263
01:30:39,797 --> 01:30:41,527
(Quiet)

2264
01:30:43,067 --> 01:30:44,747
Is there anyone who wants to get splashed?

2265
01:30:46,197 --> 01:30:48,137
(Approaching)

2266
01:30:49,867 --> 01:30:51,337
Do you want to get splashed?

2267
01:30:52,507 --> 01:30:55,037
(Do you want to get splashed?)

2268
01:30:55,377 --> 01:30:56,646
I'm going to splash you.

2269
01:30:56,647 --> 01:30:58,106
(No.)

2270
01:30:58,107 --> 01:30:59,817
I'm going to spray your feet.

2271
01:31:00,977 --> 01:31:05,887
(Stepping backward, surprised by her madness)

2272
01:31:06,117 --> 01:31:08,286
Gosh. It's nice and cool. Good.

2273
01:31:08,287 --> 01:31:09,787
(Sun Young's having fun.)

2274
01:31:10,657 --> 01:31:16,097
(Thanks to her, the siblings' yard cooled off.)

2275
01:31:16,727 --> 01:31:17,996
(Meanwhile, Jung Ah is chopping something.)

2276
01:31:17,997 --> 01:31:19,027
What is that?

2277
01:31:19,697 --> 01:31:22,197
I'm going to make seasoned green peppers.

2278
01:31:22,707 --> 01:31:23,766
(A side dish to enjoy with the dishes for the showdown)

2279
01:31:23,767 --> 01:31:25,413
- Are you going to use all of these? - It's going to be a side dish. Yes.

2280
01:31:25,437 --> 01:31:27,336
- I'll chop these. - No, I can do it later.

2281
01:31:27,337 --> 01:31:29,507
How should I chop these?

2282
01:31:29,807 --> 01:31:31,306
- Not too thick. - Okay.

2283
01:31:31,307 --> 01:31:32,627
Because we'll have it right away.

2284
01:31:32,717 --> 01:31:34,577
(Order taken!)

2285
01:31:34,747 --> 01:31:35,747
(Chopping)

2286
01:31:35,748 --> 01:31:38,487
(Cutting)

2287
01:31:39,357 --> 01:31:42,386
(They're in the same kitchen, )

2288
01:31:42,387 --> 01:31:44,387
(but they're at different speeds.)

2289
01:31:44,927 --> 01:31:46,847
I'm good at chopping. Don't you think, everyone?

2290
01:31:47,527 --> 01:31:49,797
I'm not good at cooking, but I'm good at chopping.

2291
01:31:50,827 --> 01:31:52,766
True. But be careful with your hands.

2292
01:31:52,767 --> 01:31:55,397
I'm scared because you're so fast.

2293
01:31:55,497 --> 01:31:56,567
- Really? - Yes.

2294
01:31:56,907 --> 01:31:58,666
I can't chop that fast because I'm scared.

2295
01:31:58,667 --> 01:31:59,677
I see. Really?

2296
01:32:00,677 --> 01:32:02,546
- It's frustrating when I'm slow. - Do it like this.

2297
01:32:02,547 --> 01:32:04,667
(She's Wasp Sun Young when it comes to chopping too.)

2298
01:32:06,077 --> 01:32:09,447
(Still chopping at lightning speed)

2299
01:32:09,847 --> 01:32:12,687
(Thanks to Wasp Sun Young, they're done chopping quickly.)

2300
01:32:12,787 --> 01:32:14,116
Gosh. I love this side dish.

2301
01:32:14,117 --> 01:32:15,763
(It's time to make the seasoning for the dish Sun Young likes.)

2302
01:32:15,787 --> 01:32:17,526
(Starting with flavorful doenjang)

2303
01:32:17,527 --> 01:32:19,057
(4 tablespoons)

2304
01:32:19,497 --> 01:32:21,897
(Squeezing starch syrup in)

2305
01:32:22,397 --> 01:32:25,067
(2 tablespoons of minced garlic, 4 tablespoons of chili powder)

2306
01:32:25,567 --> 01:32:27,937
(Adding nutty flavor with sesame oil)

2307
01:32:28,237 --> 01:32:31,267
(Increasing the nutty flavor with lots of sesame)

2308
01:32:32,007 --> 01:32:34,407
(The seasoning, measured out in a flash, )

2309
01:32:35,137 --> 01:32:39,277
(is mixed well, so the flavors can blend in together.)

2310
01:32:41,317 --> 01:32:43,616
(Adding the sauce to the green peppers and onions...)

2311
01:32:43,617 --> 01:32:45,147
(without hesitation)

2312
01:32:46,887 --> 01:32:48,686
(She mixes them well...)

2313
01:32:48,687 --> 01:32:51,827
(so that the ingredients are evenly coated in seasoning.)

2314
01:32:52,557 --> 01:32:54,997
(She gives it a try.)

2315
01:32:55,797 --> 01:32:57,567
(Nodding with satisfaction)

2316
01:32:57,827 --> 01:32:59,867
Good. I need a container.

2317
01:33:01,167 --> 01:33:03,007
(After putting it in a container, )

2318
01:33:03,837 --> 01:33:07,207
(crunchy and salty seasoned green peppers are ready.)

2319
01:33:07,407 --> 01:33:08,436
Let's go.

2320
01:33:08,437 --> 01:33:09,476
You can go first.

2321
01:33:09,477 --> 01:33:11,347
- I'll join you after this. - Okay.

2322
01:33:13,147 --> 01:33:16,547
(Sun Young heads to the mural on a bicycle.)

2323
01:33:17,887 --> 01:33:19,417
Okay, let's go!

2324
01:33:20,117 --> 01:33:22,157
(Giggling)

2325
01:33:22,487 --> 01:33:25,127
It's fun to cycle after a long time.

2326
01:33:25,457 --> 01:33:26,457
Yes.

2327
01:33:26,797 --> 01:33:30,267
(Sun Young is excited like a child about cycling after a long time.)

2328
01:33:31,597 --> 01:33:33,166
Catch up quickly!

2329
01:33:33,167 --> 01:33:34,737
(Talking to the drone)

2330
01:33:35,867 --> 01:33:38,837
(I'm here!)

2331
01:33:39,637 --> 01:33:40,906
Fly faster!

2332
01:33:40,907 --> 01:33:42,807
(Fly faster and catch me.)

2333
01:33:43,307 --> 01:33:44,647
Fly faster!

2334
01:33:45,177 --> 01:33:47,517
(Was that Sun Young's voice?)

2335
01:33:47,777 --> 01:33:50,786
It's fun to cycle. It's been ages since I last cycled!

2336
01:33:50,787 --> 01:33:52,687
This is fun.

2337
01:33:53,187 --> 01:33:56,326
Cycling is so fun.

2338
01:33:56,327 --> 01:33:57,887
(She arrives with a burst of dopamine.)

2339
01:33:58,357 --> 01:34:00,856
Gosh, this is so nice.

2340
01:34:00,857 --> 01:34:02,843
(Another burst of dopamine when she sees the mural)

2341
01:34:02,867 --> 01:34:03,867
This is so pretty.

2342
01:34:05,597 --> 01:34:07,237
- What should I paint now? - This.

2343
01:34:07,797 --> 01:34:08,866
This.

2344
01:34:08,867 --> 01:34:10,166
(Sun Young in charge of coloring the fish)

2345
01:34:10,167 --> 01:34:11,707
Where? I'll start painting first.

2346
01:34:12,837 --> 01:34:13,877
Here.

2347
01:34:14,177 --> 01:34:17,407
(She paints carefully while imagining orange fish.)

2348
01:34:18,977 --> 01:34:21,917
(Immersed completely)

2349
01:34:22,547 --> 01:34:27,217
(They add life to the wall with variety of colors.)

2350
01:34:27,887 --> 01:34:28,957
This is fun.

2351
01:34:31,127 --> 01:34:32,656
I don't really get to paint when I'm alone.

2352
01:34:32,657 --> 01:34:35,297
(Yoon Seo is happy to paint for the first time in a while.)

2353
01:34:35,827 --> 01:34:38,627
It's nice to draw after a while, right, Sang Hun?

2354
01:34:39,767 --> 01:34:40,896
You can empty your mind...

2355
01:34:40,897 --> 01:34:42,037
- Exactly. - When you paint.

2356
01:34:42,597 --> 01:34:45,407
I recommend painting to those who has a lot of stress.

2357
01:34:45,607 --> 01:34:47,577
Yes. For 2 to 3 years,

2358
01:34:47,907 --> 01:34:50,447
I just played music and painted...

2359
01:34:51,407 --> 01:34:52,646
at home.

2360
01:34:52,647 --> 01:34:54,553
(Drawing was a hobby and a comfort to Sun Young too.)

2361
01:34:54,577 --> 01:34:56,247
But look. It's very funny.

2362
01:34:57,587 --> 01:35:00,787
What if you draw wrongly?

2363
01:35:01,587 --> 01:35:04,286
- You paint over it. - Yes, paint over it and draw again.

2364
01:35:04,287 --> 01:35:05,326
- Yes. - You can make mistakes...

2365
01:35:05,327 --> 01:35:06,327
in your life.

2366
01:35:06,597 --> 01:35:08,997
- Of course. - You can start over.

2367
01:35:10,067 --> 01:35:12,096
(After his wise words, he focuses on painting again.)

2368
01:35:12,097 --> 01:35:13,167
Hear, hear.

2369
01:35:13,667 --> 01:35:16,367
You can make mistakes as you live.

2370
01:35:17,437 --> 01:35:18,966
This is fun.

2371
01:35:18,967 --> 01:35:20,647
It's my first time painting, and it's fun.

2372
01:35:20,977 --> 01:35:24,006
- It's my first time too. - I feel a sense of responsibility.

2373
01:35:24,007 --> 01:35:25,947
(They're getting immersed in it.)

2374
01:35:26,947 --> 01:35:28,017
(A shout)

2375
01:35:28,977 --> 01:35:30,047
(Shouting)

2376
01:35:30,117 --> 01:35:31,186
Here she comes.

2377
01:35:31,187 --> 01:35:32,217
(Laughing)

2378
01:35:32,957 --> 01:35:34,016
My goodness.

2379
01:35:34,017 --> 01:35:35,497
(Jung Ah rides the bicycle unstably.)

2380
01:35:36,017 --> 01:35:38,987
(She rides very slowly and carefully.)

2381
01:35:40,727 --> 01:35:42,767
(Her heart drops when she rides over a bump.)

2382
01:35:43,997 --> 01:35:45,296
(The seniors greet her.)

2383
01:35:45,297 --> 01:35:46,697
I'm bad at cycling.

2384
01:35:46,937 --> 01:35:48,337
I'm bad at cycling.

2385
01:35:49,097 --> 01:35:50,536
I'm bad at it. I can't stop.

2386
01:35:50,537 --> 01:35:52,307
(I'm sorry, but I'll ride ahead.)

2387
01:35:52,977 --> 01:35:55,677
(Struggling)

2388
01:35:56,407 --> 01:35:57,476
My gosh.

2389
01:35:57,477 --> 01:35:58,977
(She barely makes it to the mural.)

2390
01:35:59,747 --> 01:36:02,077
(She regains her confidence once she's back on her feet.)

2391
01:36:02,747 --> 01:36:04,087
You're all so cool.

2392
01:36:05,187 --> 01:36:06,217
(Squealing)

2393
01:36:06,987 --> 01:36:08,316
- You painted a lot. - Yes.

2394
01:36:08,317 --> 01:36:09,827
- Right? - Yes.

2395
01:36:10,527 --> 01:36:11,587
What should I paint?

2396
01:36:11,787 --> 01:36:14,697
Jung Ah, it's a starfish down there.

2397
01:36:15,727 --> 01:36:18,026
Color it in one color. Orange?

2398
01:36:18,027 --> 01:36:19,787
- Sounds good. - I'll mix the paint for you.

2399
01:36:20,067 --> 01:36:22,697
(Excited to paint for the first time)

2400
01:36:23,167 --> 01:36:24,437
- Here's orange. - Okay.

2401
01:36:24,737 --> 01:36:27,507
It's pretty. Orange here.

2402
01:36:28,377 --> 01:36:30,907
I've waited for you for so long, orange.

2403
01:36:32,377 --> 01:36:38,017
(The 1st painting experience she's waited for 55 years)

2404
01:36:41,757 --> 01:36:44,457
- Yoon Seo, is this how I do it? - Yes, it looks great.

2405
01:36:44,627 --> 01:36:45,687
- Does it? - Yes.

2406
01:36:46,397 --> 01:36:49,097
(A skilled newbie)

2407
01:36:50,267 --> 01:36:52,167
- How is this, teacher? - Sorry?

2408
01:36:52,897 --> 01:36:54,796
- It's so cute. - Does the seagull look okay?

2409
01:36:54,797 --> 01:36:55,866
Yes. You're talented.

2410
01:36:55,867 --> 01:36:56,867
(Top student You Seok's work)

2411
01:36:56,868 --> 01:36:58,043
- I got a compliment. - It's so good.

2412
01:36:58,067 --> 01:36:59,906
Painting the turtle is going to be really difficult.

2413
01:36:59,907 --> 01:37:01,507
No, I think you can do it.

2414
01:37:01,777 --> 01:37:03,847
(It's time to paint the turtle.)

2415
01:37:04,307 --> 01:37:06,067
- I'm scared to work on the turtle. - Do it.

2416
01:37:07,577 --> 01:37:08,947
- Teacher Yoon Seo. - Yes?

2417
01:37:09,047 --> 01:37:11,316
How should I color...

2418
01:37:11,317 --> 01:37:12,347
the turtle?

2419
01:37:12,687 --> 01:37:13,717
By mixing the paint.

2420
01:37:14,787 --> 01:37:17,457
There should be green paint. Did you open up everything?

2421
01:37:18,627 --> 01:37:21,107
It's so funny to see you guys speaking formally when you work.

2422
01:37:22,797 --> 01:37:24,366
(Why do you guys do that?)

2423
01:37:24,367 --> 01:37:25,967
- Now, I... - It's so funny.

2424
01:37:26,067 --> 01:37:28,666
I'm treating her as a teacher.

2425
01:37:28,667 --> 01:37:30,666
This is so funny.

2426
01:37:30,667 --> 01:37:31,707
She's my teacher.

2427
01:37:31,807 --> 01:37:34,106
- You're all so good. - This is so nice.

2428
01:37:34,107 --> 01:37:35,807
You Seok is really good too.

2429
01:37:36,447 --> 01:37:38,647
- You're the best. - No, I...

2430
01:37:39,547 --> 01:37:40,676
I'm painting it.

2431
01:37:40,677 --> 01:37:42,557
(Yoon Seo is painting the boat all by herself.)

2432
01:37:42,817 --> 01:37:44,747
(Stroke)

2433
01:37:45,047 --> 01:37:47,187
It's my first time working on such a big project too.

2434
01:37:49,087 --> 01:37:50,156
It looks nice.

2435
01:37:50,157 --> 01:37:51,433
(Under pressure, Yoon Seo quietly focuses on her work.)

2436
01:37:51,457 --> 01:37:52,457
The boat looks nice.

2437
01:37:53,797 --> 01:37:55,397
I'm using light green.

2438
01:37:57,127 --> 01:38:00,297
(This time, she starts painting without a sketch.)

2439
01:38:01,037 --> 01:38:02,536
It really makes me focus.

2440
01:38:02,537 --> 01:38:03,606
(She paints confidently even without a sketch.)

2441
01:38:03,607 --> 01:38:06,066
Gosh, Yoon Seo.

2442
01:38:06,067 --> 01:38:07,837
You're so...

2443
01:38:08,507 --> 01:38:10,207
I need to paint it yellow.

2444
01:38:10,647 --> 01:38:13,677
- Yellow? Where? - There,

2445
01:38:14,647 --> 01:38:17,587
(Bob Ross paints it yellow.)

2446
01:38:18,047 --> 01:38:19,786
And a person here.

2447
01:38:19,787 --> 01:38:21,433
(Thanks to the help, she picks up her pace.)

2448
01:38:21,457 --> 01:38:23,587
(Staring)

2449
01:38:24,027 --> 01:38:26,227
(Jung Ah finishes painting the starfish.)

2450
01:38:27,297 --> 01:38:28,927
Should I paint another starfish?

2451
01:38:29,427 --> 01:38:32,327
- What color should I use? - Your skirt's color.

2452
01:38:33,037 --> 01:38:35,797
Should I mix the paint to make this color?

2453
01:38:37,237 --> 01:38:39,437
(Let's see.)

2454
01:38:40,307 --> 01:38:43,447
(Jung Ah mixes the paint to make her skirt's color.)

2455
01:38:44,047 --> 01:38:45,076
- Here. - Yes.

2456
01:38:45,077 --> 01:38:46,106
(Although it's her first time, she mixes the colors boldly.)

2457
01:38:46,107 --> 01:38:47,177
Stop.

2458
01:38:47,377 --> 01:38:49,647
(Skillful)

2459
01:38:50,087 --> 01:38:52,617
(Let's try.)

2460
01:38:52,817 --> 01:38:55,756
(Painting the starfish with the color she made)

2461
01:38:55,757 --> 01:38:57,656
Everyone is excited and enthusiastic.

2462
01:38:57,657 --> 01:38:59,527
It's really fun to draw.

2463
01:39:00,097 --> 01:39:01,927
(Let me see.)

2464
01:39:02,197 --> 01:39:04,567
- Sun Young, is the color okay? - Sorry?

2465
01:39:04,997 --> 01:39:06,067
It's fantastic.

2466
01:39:07,567 --> 01:39:09,567
- I made it. - I think you have a knack for it.

2467
01:39:10,937 --> 01:39:13,207
- Jung Ah, it's so pretty. - What?

2468
01:39:13,577 --> 01:39:15,036
Good job mixing the colors.

2469
01:39:15,037 --> 01:39:16,477
(A perfect replication of her skirt)

2470
01:39:17,347 --> 01:39:18,406
In here...

2471
01:39:18,407 --> 01:39:19,846
(With the praises motivating her...)

2472
01:39:19,847 --> 01:39:20,916
It's pretty.

2473
01:39:20,917 --> 01:39:22,253
(She finishes the second starfish.)

2474
01:39:22,277 --> 01:39:25,187
- It's fun, isn't it? - Yes, it's fun.

2475
01:39:26,047 --> 01:39:28,417
(Since it's fun, she paints another one.)

2476
01:39:28,957 --> 01:39:31,287
(This time with Sun Young)

2477
01:39:31,557 --> 01:39:34,077
(She suddenly takes a few steps back in the midst of painting.)

2478
01:39:34,157 --> 01:39:36,127
(Staring)

2479
01:39:36,767 --> 01:39:38,967
(She focuses on painting again.)

2480
01:39:39,597 --> 01:39:41,767
(Actually no, she stares at it again.)

2481
01:39:42,367 --> 01:39:45,267
(And she paints again.)

2482
01:39:45,867 --> 01:39:49,136
(And she steps back again.)

2483
01:39:49,137 --> 01:39:51,177
- Where do you keep going? - I...

2484
01:39:51,677 --> 01:39:52,677
What do you keep...

2485
01:39:53,047 --> 01:39:55,077
- I want to see if I did well. - Goodness.

2486
01:39:55,577 --> 01:39:58,046
- See what? - If I did well.

2487
01:39:58,047 --> 01:40:00,086
- My goodness. - It's fascinating.

2488
01:40:00,087 --> 01:40:01,887
- My goodness. - That I did this.

2489
01:40:04,387 --> 01:40:06,497
I'd never paint on my own.

2490
01:40:06,957 --> 01:40:09,967
I think this is great. Painting.

2491
01:40:10,527 --> 01:40:12,727
Everyone is so serious about it.

2492
01:40:13,297 --> 01:40:15,578
I'll feel really proud of myself when I'm done with this.

2493
01:40:15,867 --> 01:40:17,313
- I'm already feeling proud. - Exactly.

2494
01:40:17,337 --> 01:40:18,817
Let's come back here ten years later.

2495
01:40:20,507 --> 01:40:21,507
When I'm 65?

2496
01:40:21,937 --> 01:40:23,877
Why not? You'll still be alive.

2497
01:40:24,207 --> 01:40:25,207
I should be alive.

2498
01:40:25,507 --> 01:40:27,217
But wouldn't I be busy?

2499
01:40:27,517 --> 01:40:29,317
You can make time to visit here, I'm sure.

2500
01:40:29,417 --> 01:40:32,087
(Come with me.)

2501
01:40:32,717 --> 01:40:34,486
Sure, ten years later.

2502
01:40:34,487 --> 01:40:36,607
(They work hard with the promises of 10 years later.)

2503
01:40:36,957 --> 01:40:37,957
It's so pretty.

2504
01:40:40,357 --> 01:40:42,796
Let's stop here and add the details tomorrow.

2505
01:40:42,797 --> 01:40:44,397
(Today's mural painting is almost done.)

2506
01:40:44,967 --> 01:40:45,967
I'm done.

2507
01:40:47,137 --> 01:40:48,897
We just need to finish this.

2508
01:40:50,367 --> 01:40:52,036
(A turtle in green costume...)

2509
01:40:52,037 --> 01:40:55,037
(and 2 colorful fish)

2510
01:40:55,507 --> 01:40:57,007
(Plus a cool boat Yoon Seo drew)

2511
01:40:57,307 --> 01:40:59,346
- Shall we stop and go? - Let's go.

2512
01:40:59,347 --> 01:41:00,377
- Yes. - Yes.

2513
01:41:00,817 --> 01:41:02,576
(The mural which only had blue waves...)

2514
01:41:02,577 --> 01:41:04,887
(is now filled with various colors.)

2515
01:41:05,447 --> 01:41:07,287
We both collaborate and compete today.

2516
01:41:08,157 --> 01:41:10,287
We collaborated, but from now on, we're enemies.

2517
01:41:13,727 --> 01:41:14,997
Culinary showdown.

2518
01:41:15,497 --> 01:41:16,897
Let's do it now.

2519
01:41:17,667 --> 01:41:19,387
(The siblings have gathered in the yard...)

2520
01:41:20,067 --> 01:41:21,707
(with 5 suspicious-looking plastic bags.)

2521
01:41:22,097 --> 01:41:24,337
(In the bags are the odd outfits they each prepared.)

2522
01:41:24,637 --> 01:41:27,207
(They're randomly placed unbeknownst to the owners.)

2523
01:41:27,407 --> 01:41:29,107
How do you decide who picks first?

2524
01:41:29,207 --> 01:41:30,576
- Rock, paper, scissors? - Rock, paper, scissors.

2525
01:41:30,577 --> 01:41:31,906
- Let's play rock, paper, scissors. - Rock, paper...

2526
01:41:31,907 --> 01:41:33,853
- Rock, paper, scissors. - Rock, paper, scissors.

2527
01:41:33,877 --> 01:41:35,153
- Rock, paper, scissors. - Rock, paper, scissors.

2528
01:41:35,177 --> 01:41:36,216
- Scissors. - Scissors.

2529
01:41:36,217 --> 01:41:38,947
(Jung Ah and You Seok win.)

2530
01:41:39,117 --> 01:41:40,316
- Rock, paper, scissors. - Scissors.

2531
01:41:40,317 --> 01:41:41,517
You first. First and second.

2532
01:41:41,617 --> 01:41:43,187
Play or lose, rock, paper, scissors.

2533
01:41:43,557 --> 01:41:44,587
Come on.

2534
01:41:44,787 --> 01:41:45,787
Rock, paper, scissors.

2535
01:41:45,788 --> 01:41:47,457
(5th, Sang Hun, 4th, Sun Young)

2536
01:41:47,727 --> 01:41:50,197
(Jung Ah picks first.)

2537
01:41:50,397 --> 01:41:52,797
You can kind of tell what it is.

2538
01:41:53,537 --> 01:41:56,037
- I can't poke it, can I? - No.

2539
01:41:56,267 --> 01:41:58,007
I think mine will suit you.

2540
01:41:58,137 --> 01:41:59,166
(Sighs)

2541
01:41:59,167 --> 01:42:00,337
(She's serious over this.)

2542
01:42:00,977 --> 01:42:03,307
(The bags all come in different sizes.)

2543
01:42:03,577 --> 01:42:06,647
(1 is slightly thick, 2, 3, and 4 are flat, and 5 is the thickest.)

2544
01:42:07,317 --> 01:42:10,117
- Number Five looks good. - I hate thick and hot clothes.

2545
01:42:10,787 --> 01:42:13,017
(Jung Ah can't stand the heat.)

2546
01:42:14,517 --> 01:42:16,627
(She chooses the flat Number 2.)

2547
01:42:16,857 --> 01:42:18,057
(Jung Ah has made her choice.)

2548
01:42:18,257 --> 01:42:19,257
(It's You Seok's turn.)

2549
01:42:19,258 --> 01:42:20,596
Number Three looks very thin.

2550
01:42:20,597 --> 01:42:22,796
Numbers 1 and 5 look heavy.

2551
01:42:22,797 --> 01:42:24,127
I choose Number Three.

2552
01:42:24,767 --> 01:42:27,067
Ta-da. This is why rock, paper, scissors is important.

2553
01:42:27,337 --> 01:42:28,397
That looks like mine.

2554
01:42:28,637 --> 01:42:29,697
It's light.

2555
01:42:30,207 --> 01:42:31,636
Yoon Seo, I think Number Five is mine. Pick that.

2556
01:42:31,637 --> 01:42:32,666
- No. - It's really good.

2557
01:42:32,667 --> 01:42:33,737
I choose Number One.

2558
01:42:34,277 --> 01:42:36,107
(Yoon Seo chooses Number 1.)

2559
01:42:36,707 --> 01:42:39,547
(Sun Young avoids Number 5 and chooses Number 4.)

2560
01:42:39,777 --> 01:42:43,017
It looks big and stuffy.

2561
01:42:44,317 --> 01:42:45,387
Wait.

2562
01:42:45,547 --> 01:42:47,187
What's this?

2563
01:42:48,217 --> 01:42:50,257
(It doesn't feel all that bad.)

2564
01:42:51,427 --> 01:42:52,856
Do we just wear these?

